{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T21:58:28.815659", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement actions and their corresponding (row_delta, col_delta)\n  # (dy, dx) for grid traversal.\n  ACTION_TO_DELTAS = {\n      action_map['UP']: (-1, 0),\n      action_map['DOWN']: (1, 0),\n      action_map['LEFT']: (0, -1),\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (0, 1),\n  }\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive and check inventory.\n  try:\n    i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, return an empty list.\n    return []\n\n  # If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is \"grabbable\" (can be picked up by moving onto its cell)\n  # or \"non-grabbable\" (requires an explicit USE action when adjacent).\n  is_grabbable = i_primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # 2. Check for immediate collection/use if already in position.\n  # This applies primarily to non-grabbable items that need a 'USE' action.\n  # For grabbable items, the BFS will correctly lead to the item's cell\n  # and implicitly \"collect\" it by moving there.\n  if not is_grabbable and current_state.next_to(i_primitive):\n    return [USE_ACTION]\n\n  # 3. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's starting (row, col) position\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # BFS queue: stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # Set to keep track of visited grid positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # Define cells containing these indices as impassable obstacles for agent movement.\n  # These are typically non-grabbable environment features (e.g., Water, Stone, Workshops)\n  # that the agent cannot step onto.\n  obstacle_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # BFS loop continues as long as there are positions to explore in the queue.\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path_actions = q.popleft()\n    curr_row, curr_col = curr_pos\n\n    target_condition_met = False\n    final_actions = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable primitives, the goal is to move onto the cell containing it.\n      # The environment's 'step' function handles the actual \"pickup\" when the agent lands on it.\n      if grid[curr_row, curr_col, i_primitive] > 0:\n        final_actions = path_actions\n        target_condition_met = True\n    else:\n      # For non-grabbable primitives, collecting them implies interacting with them\n      # using the 'USE' action when adjacent. We check the 4-directional neighborhood\n      # (up, down, left, right) from curr_pos.\n      for d_row, d_col in ACTION_TO_DELTAS.values():\n        neighbor_row, neighbor_col = curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col\n\n        # Ensure the neighbor cell is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= neighbor_row < grid_rows and 0 <= neighbor_col < grid_cols:\n          # If the primitive is found in an adjacent cell, we can use the 'USE' action.\n          if grid[neighbor_row, neighbor_col, i_primitive] > 0:\n            final_actions = path_actions + [USE_ACTION]\n            target_condition_met = True\n            break  # Found a suitable adjacent target, no need to check other neighbors\n\n    if target_condition_met:\n      return final_actions\n\n    # If the target is not found yet, explore valid neighboring cells.\n    for action_val, (d_row, d_col) in ACTION_TO_DELTAS.items():\n      next_pos = (curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col)\n      next_row, next_col = next_pos\n\n      # 1. Check if the next position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_row < grid_rows and 0 <= next_col < grid_cols):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Check if the next position is an obstacle.\n      # An obstacle cell is one that contains any non-grabbable entity,\n      # which the agent cannot move onto.\n      is_cell_obstacle = any(grid[next_row, next_col, kind_idx] > 0 for kind_idx in obstacle_indices)\n\n      # 3. Check if the next position has already been visited.\n      # If not visited and not an obstacle, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      if next_pos not in visited and not is_cell_obstacle:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        q.append((next_pos, path_actions + [action_val]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to the primitive (or its interaction point)\n  # was found, return an empty list of actions, indicating it's unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T21:58:30.046431", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n  This function finds the shortest path to a primitive resource on the grid\n  and generates the actions required to collect it. It distinguishes between\n  'grabbable' items (collected by moving onto their cell) and\n  'non-grabbable' sources (collected by moving adjacent and using the 'USE' action).\n  The BFS search ensures the shortest path is found and correctly handles obstacles.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Initialize Action Mappings and Primitive ID\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Map movement actions to their corresponding (row_delta, col_delta) for grid traversal.\n  # (row_delta, col_delta) indicates change in (Y, X) or (row, column).\n  MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS = {\n      action_map['UP']: (-1, 0),    # Move up: decreases row index\n      action_map['DOWN']: (1, 0),   # Move down: increases row index\n      action_map['LEFT']: (0, -1),  # Move left: decreases column index\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (0, 1),  # Move right: increases column index\n  }\n\n  try:\n    i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Get Current State Information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Early exit: If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (collected by walking over its cell)\n  # or non-grabbable (requires 'USE' action when adjacent to its source).\n  is_grabbable = i_primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Get current grid and agent's starting position for the search.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting (row, col) position\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions: (height=rows, width=cols) for boundary checks.\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define cells containing these kinds as impassable obstacles for agent movement.\n  # These are typically non-grabbable environment features like 'WATER', 'STONE', or 'WORKSHOP' locations\n  # that the agent cannot step onto.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for Shortest Path\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position (row, col), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # A set to keep track of visited grid positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited_positions = {start_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_pos, path_to_curr_pos = queue.popleft()\n    curr_row, curr_col = curr_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position or its immediate neighbors satisfy the collection condition.\n    # This is the \"target check\" for the primitive based on its grabbable status.\n    target_collection_actions = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable primitives, the goal is to be *on* the cell containing the item.\n      # The environment's 'step' function handles the actual pickup when the agent lands on it.\n      if grid[curr_row, curr_col, i_primitive] > 0: # Assuming '1' or '>0' indicates presence\n        target_collection_actions = path_to_curr_pos # Path ends *on* the item.\n    else:\n      # For non-grabbable primitives (e.g., 'STONE' source for 'ROCK', 'WATER' source),\n      # collecting them implies interacting with them using the 'USE' action when adjacent.\n      # Check the 4 cardinal neighbors (up, down, left, right) from the current position.\n      for d_row, d_col in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS.values(): # Iterate over cardinal direction deltas\n        neighbor_row, neighbor_col = curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col\n        \n        # Ensure the neighbor cell is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= neighbor_row < grid_rows and 0 <= neighbor_col < grid_cols:\n          # If the primitive source is found in an adjacent cell, we can use the 'USE' action.\n          if grid[neighbor_row, neighbor_col, i_primitive] > 0:\n            target_collection_actions = path_to_curr_pos + [USE_ACTION]\n            break # Found a suitable adjacent target, no need to check other neighbors for this position.\n    \n    # If the target condition is met (primitive found or adjacent to source),\n    # return the sequence of actions to achieve it.\n    if target_collection_actions:\n      return target_collection_actions\n\n    # 4. Explore Neighbors: If the target is not found yet, expand the search to adjacent cells.\n    for action_val, (d_row, d_col) in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS.items():\n      next_row, next_col = curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col\n      next_pos = (next_row, next_col)\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure the next position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_row < grid_rows and 0 <= next_col < grid_cols):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the next position is an impassable obstacle.\n      # The agent cannot move onto cells containing any of the defined impassable kinds.\n      is_obstacle = any(grid[next_row, next_col, kind_idx] > 0 for kind_idx in impassable_kinds)\n      \n      # Check 3: Only add to the queue if the position has not been visited and is not an obstacle.\n      if next_pos not in visited_positions and not is_obstacle:\n        visited_positions.add(next_pos)\n        queue.append((next_pos, path_to_curr_pos + [action_val]))\n            \n  # If the BFS completes and no path to the primitive (or its interaction point) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable in the current scenario.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T21:59:33.163002", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "# 1. Initialize Action Mappings and Primitive ID\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Map movement actions to their corresponding (row_delta, col_delta) for grid traversal.\n  # (row_delta, col_delta) indicates change in (Y, X) or (row, column).\n  MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS = {\n      action_map['UP']: (-1, 0),    # Move up: decreases row index\n      action_map['DOWN']: (1, 0),   # Move down: increases row index\n      action_map['LEFT']: (0, -1),  # Move left: decreases column index\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (0, 1),  # Move right: increases column index\n  }\n\n  try:\n    i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Get Current State Information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Early exit: If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (collected by walking over its cell)\n  # or non-grabbable (requires 'USE' action when adjacent to its source).\n  is_grabbable = i_primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Get current grid and agent's starting position for the search.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting (row, col) position\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions: (height=rows, width=cols) for boundary checks.\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define cells containing these kinds as impassable obstacles for agent movement.\n  # These are typically non-grabbable environment features like 'WATER', 'STONE', or 'WORKSHOP' locations\n  # that the agent cannot step onto.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for Shortest Path\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position (row, col), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # A set to keep track of visited grid positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited_positions = {start_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_pos, path_to_curr_pos = queue.popleft()\n    curr_row, curr_col = curr_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position or its immediate neighbors satisfy the collection condition.\n    # This is the \"target check\" for the primitive based on its grabbable status.\n    target_collection_actions = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable primitives, the goal is to be *on* the cell containing the item.\n      # The environment's 'step' function handles the actual pickup when the agent lands on it.\n      if grid[curr_row, curr_col, i_primitive] > 0: # Assuming '1' or '>0' indicates presence\n        target_collection_actions = path_to_curr_pos # Path ends *on* the item.\n    else:\n      # For non-grabbable primitives (e.g., 'STONE' source for 'ROCK', 'WATER' source),\n      # collecting them implies interacting with them using the 'USE' action when adjacent.\n      # Check the 4 cardinal neighbors (up, down, left, right) from the current position.\n      for d_row, d_col in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS.values(): # Iterate over cardinal direction deltas\n        neighbor_row, neighbor_col = curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col\n        \n        # Ensure the neighbor cell is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= neighbor_row < grid_rows and 0 <= neighbor_col < grid_cols:\n          # If the primitive source is found in an adjacent cell, we can use the 'USE' action.\n          if grid[neighbor_row, neighbor_col, i_primitive] > 0:\n            target_collection_actions = path_to_curr_pos + [USE_ACTION]\n            break # Found a suitable adjacent target, no need to check other neighbors for this position.\n    \n    # If the target condition is met (primitive found or adjacent to source),\n    # return the sequence of actions to achieve it.\n    if target_collection_actions:\n      return target_collection_actions\n\n    # 4. Explore Neighbors: If the target is not found yet, expand the search to adjacent cells.\n    for action_val, (d_row, d_col) in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS.items():\n      next_row, next_col = curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col\n      next_pos = (next_row, next_col)\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure the next position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_row < grid_rows and 0 <= next_col < grid_cols):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the next position is an impassable obstacle.\n      # The agent cannot move onto cells containing any of the defined impassable kinds.\n      is_obstacle = any(grid[next_row, next_col, kind_idx] > 0 for kind_idx in impassable_kinds)\n      \n      # Check 3: Only add to the queue if the position has not been visited and is not an obstacle.\n      if next_pos not in visited_positions and not is_obstacle:\n        visited_positions.add(next_pos)\n        queue.append((next_pos, path_to_curr_pos + [action_val]))\n            \n  # If the BFS completes and no path to the primitive (or its interaction point) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable in the current scenario.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T21:59:34.445825", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # 1. Initialize Action Mappings and Primitive ID\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Map movement actions to their corresponding (row_delta, col_delta) for grid traversal.\n  # (row_delta, col_delta) indicates change in (Y, X) or (row, column).\n  # The direction of the move action also sets the agent's facing direction.\n  MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS = {\n      action_map['UP']: (-1, 0),    # Move up: decreases row index\n      action_map['DOWN']: (1, 0),   # Move down: increases row index\n      action_map['LEFT']: (0, -1),  # Move left: decreases column index\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (0, 1),  # Move right: increases column index\n  }\n\n  try:\n    i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Get Current State Information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Early exit: If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (collected by walking over its cell)\n  # or non-grabbable (requires 'USE' action when adjacent to its source and facing it).\n  is_grabbable = i_primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Get current grid and agent's starting position and direction for the search.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting (row, col) position\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting facing direction (an int corresponding to a move action)\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions: (height=rows, width=cols) for boundary checks.\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define cells containing these kinds as impassable obstacles for agent movement.\n  # These are typically non-grabbable environment features like 'WATER', 'STONE', or 'WORKSHOP' locations\n  # that the agent cannot step onto.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for Shortest Path considering agent direction\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position (row, col), current_direction (int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])])\n  \n  # A set to keep track of visited states (position, direction) to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited_states = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_pos, curr_dir_val, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n    curr_row, curr_col = curr_pos\n\n    # Check if the current state (position and direction) allows for collection.\n    # This is the \"target check\" for the primitive based on its grabbable status.\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable primitives, the goal is to be *on* the cell containing the item.\n      # The environment's 'step' function handles the actual pickup when the agent lands on it.\n      if grid[curr_row, curr_col, i_primitive] > 0: # Assuming '1' or '>0' indicates presence\n        return path_so_far # Path ends *on* the item.\n    else:\n      # For non-grabbable primitives, collecting implies interacting using the 'USE' action.\n      # This requires the agent to be adjacent to the source AND facing it.\n      \n      # Determine the cell directly in front of the agent based on its current direction.\n      if curr_dir_val in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS:\n          delta_row, delta_col = MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS[curr_dir_val]\n          target_source_pos = (curr_row + delta_row, curr_col + delta_col)\n\n          # Ensure the cell in front is within grid boundaries.\n          if 0 <= target_source_pos[0] < grid_rows and 0 <= target_source_pos[1] < grid_cols:\n            # If the cell in front contains the primitive source, we can use the 'USE' action.\n            if grid[target_source_pos[0], target_source_pos[1], i_primitive] > 0:\n              return path_so_far + [USE_ACTION]\n            \n    # If the target condition is not met at the current state, explore neighbors.\n    # For each possible movement action (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT):\n    for move_action_val, (d_row, d_col) in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_DELTAS.items():\n      next_pos = (curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col)\n      next_dir_val = move_action_val # The agent's direction changes to that of the last movement action.\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure the next position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_pos[0] < grid_rows and 0 <= next_pos[1] < grid_cols):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the next position is an impassable obstacle.\n      # The agent cannot move onto cells containing any of the defined impassable kinds.\n      is_obstacle = any(grid[next_pos[0], next_pos[1], kind_idx] > 0 for kind_idx in impassable_kinds)\n      \n      # If the target primitive itself is an obstacle (e.g., WATER, WORKSHOP),\n      # the agent cannot step on it. This is handled correctly by `impassable_kinds`.\n      # If the primitive is grabbable but also listed as impassable (unlikely by design),\n      # the agent would also avoid stepping on it, preventing collection.\n      # Assuming grabbable items are never in `non_grabbable_indices`.\n\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue\n\n      # Check 3: Only add to the queue if this (position, direction) state has not been visited.\n      next_state = (next_pos, next_dir_val)\n      if next_state not in visited_states:\n        visited_states.add(next_state)\n        queue.append((next_pos, next_dir_val, path_so_far + [move_action_val]))\n            \n  # If the BFS completes and no path to the primitive (or its interaction point) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable in the current scenario.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:00:17.335418", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # The requested primitive name is not recognized by the environment's cookbook.\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory. If so, no collection actions are needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Verify if the primitive is an item that can actually be 'grabbable' (picked up into inventory).\n  # Some items listed as \"primitives\" in the DSL (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP0)\n  # are environmental features not meant to be collected into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve current state information for pathfinding.\n  initial_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid.\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer action mappings from the environment for movement and 'USE'.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION),\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION),\n  ]\n\n  # 3. Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # If the cell contains at least one unit of the target primitive.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any cell that is adjacent to the target primitive.\n  # The 'USE' action in CraftWorld typically works on items in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])]) # Stores (current_position, path_taken_to_reach_here).\n  visited = {initial_pos} # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant computations.\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to (or on the same cell as)\n      # any of the primitive's known locations. This allows for the 'USE' action.\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # A cell is considered \"adjacent\" if it's within 1 unit of Manhattan distance\n          # in both x and y, forming a 3x3 square (including the center).\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent cell is found, append the 'USE' action and return\n          # the complete sequence of actions (movement path + use action).\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the next cell is traversable or an impassable obstacle.\n          # A cell is considered impassable if it contains any non-grabbable entity\n          # that is not explicitly defined as traversable (e.g., workshops, water).\n          is_impassable = False\n          for k_idx in range(num_kinds): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If there's something of kind k_idx at this cell...\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx:\n                      # If the cell contains the primitive itself, it is generally traversable,\n                      # as we might need to move onto or over it to collect.\n                      pass \n                  elif k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                      # Some non-grabbable entities are traversable (e.g., workshops, water).\n                      if k_idx in env.world.workshop_indices or k_idx == env.world.water_index:\n                          pass # Allow movement onto these specific non-grabbables\n                      else:\n                          # Other non-grabbable entities not explicitly allowed are obstacles.\n                          is_impassable = True\n                          break # This cell is blocked by an impassable object.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path if the cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive is found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position given the current grid.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:00:18.521293", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:01:45.692633", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACT_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACT_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACT_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACT_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACT_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Helper function to check if the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of (px, py)\n  # This corresponds to what CraftState.next_to would check if the agent was at (px, py).\n  def _is_primitive_in_neighborhood(px, py):\n      for dx_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx_n, py + dy_n\n              if 0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT:\n                  # Check if the primitive kind exists at this neighbor cell\n                  if grid[nx, ny, primitive_idx] > 0:\n                      return True\n      return False\n\n  queue = collections.deque()\n  # Stores (x, y, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue.append((start_x, start_y, []))\n\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add((start_x, start_y))\n\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), ACT_DOWN),   # (dx, dy), action\n      ((0, -1), ACT_UP),\n      ((1, 0), ACT_RIGHT),\n      ((-1, 0), ACT_LEFT),\n  ]\n\n  while queue:\n      curr_x, curr_y, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # If the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of the current position,\n      # then we are in a position from which we can \"USE\" to collect it.\n      if _is_primitive_in_neighborhood(curr_x, curr_y):\n          path_actions.append(ACT_USE)\n          return path_actions\n\n      # Explore neighbors\n      for (dx, dy), action in moves:\n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n          # Check grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if already visited\n          if (next_x, next_y) in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the cell (next_x, next_y) is traversable.\n          # A cell is traversable if it does NOT contain any non-grabbable item\n          # that is NOT a workshop. (Workshops are non-grabbable but are meant to be stood on).\n          is_traversable = True\n          \n          # Get all kinds present at the next cell\n          kinds_in_next_cell = np.where(grid[next_x, next_y] > 0)[0] \n\n          for k_idx in kinds_in_next_cell:\n              # If the item is non-grabbable AND it's not a workshop, it's an obstacle.\n              # Note: If the primitive itself is a non-grabbable item (e.g., WATER, STONE),\n              # we should still not traverse *onto* it, but rather get *adjacent* to it.\n              # This logic correctly marks such cells as non-traversable.\n              if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and k_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          \n          if is_traversable:\n              visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n              new_path_actions = path_actions + [action]\n              queue.append((next_x, next_y, new_path_actions))\n\n  # If no path is found after exploring all reachable cells, return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:01:46.880493", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACT_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACT_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACT_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACT_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACT_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is a type you stand ON (grabbable, workshop) or stand ADJACENT to (resource).\n  # Grabbable items (like dropped planks) and workshops are typically walked onto.\n  # Resources like WOOD, STONE, WATER are typically interacted with from an adjacent square.\n  is_stand_on_target = (primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices or\n                        primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  queue = collections.deque()\n  # Stores (x, y, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue.append((start_x, start_y, []))\n\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add((start_x, start_y))\n\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), ACT_DOWN),\n      ((0, -1), ACT_UP),\n      ((1, 0), ACT_RIGHT),\n      ((-1, 0), ACT_LEFT),\n  ]\n\n  while queue:\n      curr_x, curr_y, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Goal Check ---\n      if is_stand_on_target:\n          # If the primitive is grabbable (e.g., PLANK) or a workshop, agent needs to be ON its cell.\n          if grid[curr_x, curr_y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              path_actions.append(ACT_USE)\n              return path_actions\n      else:\n          # If the primitive is a resource (e.g., WOOD, STONE, WATER), agent needs to be ADJACENT to it.\n          # The BFS traversability will ensure the agent doesn't path onto these obstacles.\n          # Check if curr_x, curr_y is adjacent to the primitive_idx.\n          found_adjacent_primitive = False\n          for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                  check_x, check_y = curr_x + dx_adj, curr_y + dy_adj\n                  if 0 <= check_x < WIDTH and 0 <= check_y < HEIGHT:\n                      if grid[check_x, check_y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n                          found_adjacent_primitive = True\n                          break\n              if found_adjacent_primitive:\n                  break\n          \n          if found_adjacent_primitive:\n              path_actions.append(ACT_USE)\n              return path_actions\n\n      # --- Explore neighbors ---\n      for (dx_move, dy_move), action in moves:\n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx_move, curr_y + dy_move\n\n          # Check grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if already visited\n          if (next_x, next_y) in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # Check traversability of the next cell (next_x, next_y)\n          is_traversable = True\n          kinds_in_cell = np.where(grid[next_x, next_y] > 0)[0] \n\n          for k_idx in kinds_in_cell:\n              # A cell is NOT traversable if it contains a non-grabbable item that is NOT a workshop.\n              # This includes resources like WOOD, STONE, WATER, IRON, GRASS, ROCK, GOLD, GEM.\n              # Grabbable items (e.g., 'plank' on the ground) and workshops ARE traversable.\n              if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and k_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          \n          if is_traversable:\n              visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n              new_path_actions = path_actions + [action]\n              queue.append((next_x, next_y, new_path_actions))\n\n  # If no path is found after exploring all reachable cells, return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:02:53.955478", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Ensure that the primitive is actually \"grabbable\" (i.e., can be collected into the agent's inventory).\n  # If the primitive is a non-grabbable entity like a workshop or boundary,\n  # this function, designed for 'collection', should not attempt to 'collect' it.\n  if i_primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  width, height, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Mapping of (dr, dc) to action for moving\n  move_deltas = {\n      (1, 0): DOWN,  # (delta_row, delta_col) for DOWN\n      (-1, 0): UP,   # (delta_row, delta_col) for UP\n      (0, -1): LEFT, # (delta_row, delta_col) for LEFT\n      (0, 1): RIGHT, # (delta_row, delta_col) for RIGHT\n  }\n\n  # First, check if already in a position to collect the primitive\n  if current_state.next_to(i_primitive):\n    return [USE]\n  \n  # Define explicitly impassable entity kinds.\n  # Water is known to be impassable. Boundary is also typically impassable for movement.\n  impassable_kinds_indices = {env.world.water_index}\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in env.world.cookbook.index:\n      impassable_kinds_indices.add(env.world.cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  # Note: workshop_indices are non-grabbable but are generally walkable,\n  # so they are not included in impassable_kinds_indices.\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell is traversable for the agent.\n  # A cell is traversable if it's within grid bounds and does not contain any known impassable entity.\n  def is_cell_traversable(r, c):\n      # Check bounds\n      if not (0 <= r < width and 0 <= c < height):\n          return False \n      # Check if the cell contains any impassable obstacle\n      for idx in impassable_kinds_indices:\n          if grid[r, c, idx] > 0:\n              return False \n      return True\n\n  # BFS for shortest path to a position from which the primitive can be 'USE'd\n  queue = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) # (position, list_of_actions_to_reach_position)\n  visited = {current_pos} # Set of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  while queue:\n    (r, c), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current position (r, c) is a goal state for BFS:\n    # A goal state is any position from which the agent can immediately 'USE'\n    # to collect the target primitive. This means the primitive must be in the\n    # 3x3 neighborhood of (r, c) (including (r,c) itself).\n    is_adjacent_or_on_primitive = False\n    for dr_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dc_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            check_r, check_c = r + dr_check, c + dc_check\n            # Check if neighbor is within bounds and contains the primitive\n            if (0 <= check_r < width and 0 <= check_c < height and \n                grid[check_r, check_c, i_primitive] > 0):\n                is_adjacent_or_on_primitive = True\n                break\n        if is_adjacent_or_on_primitive:\n            break\n\n    if is_adjacent_or_on_primitive:\n        # Found path to a position where the primitive is in range for USE.\n        return path + [USE] \n\n    # Explore valid neighbors (Up, Down, Left, Right)\n    # The order of exploration does not matter for shortest path in unweighted graph\n    for dr, dc in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]: # (delta_row, delta_col)\n      nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Next row, next column\n\n      if (nr, nc) not in visited and is_cell_traversable(nr, nc):\n        visited.add((nr, nc))\n        action_to_take = move_deltas[(dr, dc)]\n        queue.append(((nr, nc), path + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If no path found after exhausting the BFS queue (primitive is unreachable)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:02:55.050316", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Ensure that the primitive is actually \"grabbable\" (i.e., can be collected into the agent's inventory).\n  # If the primitive is a non-grabbable entity like a workshop or boundary,\n  # this function, designed for 'collection', should not attempt to 'collect' it.\n  if i_primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  width, height, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Mapping of (dr, dc) to action for moving\n  move_deltas = {\n      (1, 0): DOWN,\n      (-1, 0): UP,\n      (0, -1): LEFT,\n      (0, 1): RIGHT,\n  }\n\n  # First, check if already in a position to collect the primitive\n  if current_state.next_to(i_primitive):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # Identify all kinds that act as impassable terrain.\n  # This typically includes water and other non-grabbable environment elements like workshops or boundaries.\n  # The assumption here is that all non-grabbable entities are obstacles to movement.\n  impassable_kinds = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n  \n  # Helper function to check if a cell is traversable for the agent.\n  # A cell is traversable if it's within grid bounds and does not contain any impassable kind.\n  def is_cell_traversable(r, c):\n      if not (0 <= r < width and 0 <= c < height):\n          return False # Out of bounds\n      # Check if this cell contains any of the known impassable kinds\n      for k_impassable in impassable_kinds:\n          if grid[r, c, k_impassable] > 0:\n              return False # Contains an impassable entity, so not traversable\n      return True\n\n  # BFS for shortest path to a position from which the primitive can be 'USE'd\n  queue = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) # (position, list_of_actions)\n  visited = {current_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n    (r, c), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current position (r, c) is a goal state for BFS:\n    # A goal state is any position from which the agent can immediately 'USE'\n    # to collect the target primitive. This means the primitive must be in the\n    # 3x3 neighborhood of (r, c).\n    # This check is equivalent to `current_state.at_position(r, c).next_to(i_primitive)`\n    # if we could easily simulate state at (r,c).\n    is_adjacent_or_on_primitive = False\n    for dr_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dc_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            check_r, check_c = r + dr_check, c + dc_check\n            # Check if neighbor is within bounds and contains the primitive\n            if (0 <= check_r < width and 0 <= check_c < height and \n                grid[check_r, check_c, i_primitive] > 0):\n                is_adjacent_or_on_primitive = True\n                break\n        if is_adjacent_or_on_primitive:\n            break\n\n    if is_adjacent_or_on_primitive:\n        return path + [USE] # Found path to a position where we can USE.\n\n    # Explore valid neighbors (Up, Down, Left, Right)\n    for dr, dc in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]:\n      nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Next row, next column\n\n      if (nr, nc) not in visited and is_cell_traversable(nr, nc):\n        visited.add((nr, nc))\n        action_to_take = move_deltas[(dr, dc)]\n        queue.append(((nr, nc), path + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If no path found after exhausting the BFS queue\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T22:04:03.354851", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = env.action_specs()\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  try:\n    i_primitive = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, return an empty list.\n    return []\n\n  # Get the current state of the environment.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Retrieve relevant observations.\n  inventory = current_state.inventory\n  features_ego = current_state.features_dict()['features_ego'] # Egocentric view (agent at center)\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is 'grabbable' (can be picked up by moving onto its cell).\n  is_grabbable = i_primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # --- Step 1: Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory. ---\n  if inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n    return [] # Already collected, no actions needed.\n\n  # --- Step 2: Check if the primitive is in the immediate 3x3 neighborhood. ---\n  # If it's a non-grabbable primitive (e.g., 'STONE' source, 'WATER' source),\n  # we need to use the 'USE' action when adjacent to it.\n  # If it's grabbable and adjacent, we need to move towards it (handled in Step 3).\n  if current_state.next_to(i_primitive) and not is_grabbable:\n      return [actions['USE']]\n\n  # --- Step 3: Scan the egocentric view for the closest visible primitive and move towards it. ---\n  ego_rows, ego_cols, _ = features_ego.shape\n  center_r, center_c = ego_rows // 2, ego_cols // 2 # Agent's position in the egocentric view\n\n  best_action_to_move = None\n  min_dist_sq = float('inf') # Tracks squared Euclidean distance to find the closest primitive\n\n  # Iterate through the egocentric view (grid slice around the agent).\n  for r in range(ego_rows):\n    for c in range(ego_cols):\n      # If the primitive is found at (r, c) in the egocentric view.\n      if features_ego[r, c, i_primitive] == 1:\n        # Calculate squared Euclidean distance from the agent's center.\n        dist_sq = (r - center_r)**2 + (c - center_c)**2\n        \n        # We want to move towards any grabbable primitive, or towards a non-grabbable\n        # primitive that is not yet directly adjacent (i.e., not handled by Step 2).\n        # A non-grabbable that is 'next_to' (adjacent, dist_sq 0, 1, or 2) would have been handled by Step 2.\n        # So, if it's non-grabbable AND we reach this step, it must be farther than 'adjacent'.\n        if is_grabbable or dist_sq > 2: # dist_sq > 2 means it's outside the 3x3 immediate neighborhood (excluding corners for dist 2)\n            if dist_sq < min_dist_sq:\n              min_dist_sq = dist_sq\n              \n              # Determine the relative movement needed from agent's center to (r, c).\n              # Assumes features_ego is oriented relative to the agent's current direction\n              # (e.g., r < center_r means \"forward\", c < center_c means \"left\").\n              delta_r = r - center_r \n              delta_c = c - center_c\n\n              # Prioritize movement in the direction with the largest absolute displacement.\n              # If absolute displacements are equal, prioritize vertical movement (UP/DOWN).\n              if abs(delta_r) >= abs(delta_c):\n                if delta_r < 0:\n                  best_action_to_move = actions['UP']\n                else: # delta_r > 0\n                  best_action_to_move = actions['DOWN']\n              else: # abs(delta_c) > abs(delta_r)\n                if delta_c < 0:\n                  best_action_to_move = actions['LEFT']\n                else: # delta_c > 0\n                  best_action_to_move = actions['RIGHT']\n\n  # If a primitive was found in the egocentric view and a move was determined.\n  if best_action_to_move is not None:\n    return [best_action_to_move]\n\n  # --- Step 4: If the primitive is not in inventory, not adjacent, and not visible, ---\n  # perform a systematic exploration move to search for it.\n  # This is an improvement over `v1`'s simple `[actions['RIGHT']]` default.\n  \n  # Get agent's current global position and grid dimensions\n  curr_row, curr_col = current_state.pos\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n  # Obstacles are non-grabbable entities the agent cannot move onto.\n  obstacle_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) \n\n  # Define a prioritized order for exploration actions (e.g., North, East, South, West).\n  # The first valid, non-obstacle move in this sequence will be chosen.\n  exploration_order = [\n      (actions['UP'],    (-1, 0)), # (action, (delta_row, delta_col))\n      (actions['RIGHT'], (0, 1)),\n      (actions['DOWN'],  (1, 0)),\n      (actions['LEFT'],  (0, -1)),\n  ]\n\n  for action_choice, (d_row, d_col) in exploration_order:\n      next_row, next_col = curr_row + d_row, curr_col + d_col\n\n      # Check if the potential next position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_row < grid_rows and 0 <= next_col < grid_cols):\n          continue # Out of bounds, try the next action in the order.\n\n      # Check if the potential next position contains an obstacle.\n      is_cell_obstacle = False\n      for kind_idx in obstacle_indices:\n          if current_state.grid[next_row, next_col, kind_idx] == 1:\n              is_cell_obstacle = True\n              break\n      \n      # If the next position is within bounds and not an obstacle, take this action.\n      if not is_cell_obstacle:\n          return [action_choice] \n\n  # --- Step 5: If no valid exploration move can be found (e.g., agent is completely trapped). ---\n  return [] # Indicate that no action can be taken to collect the primitive.", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
