{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:36:49.848277", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n  This function implements a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest\n  sequence of actions (movements and a final 'USE' action) required to collect\n  a specified primitive resource in the CraftWorld environment.\n\n  Improvements over `v1`:\n  - More explicit handling and comments regarding `Index.index` behavior,\n    confirming it doesn't raise `KeyError` for valid DSL primitives.\n  - Clearer structure and comments for each step of the collection logic.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation.\n      primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of action indices (integers) to execute in the environment.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is already collected,\n                 is non-grabbable, or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive string from the cookbook's index.\n  # The `Index.index()` method from the `Cookbook` class will always return an\n  # integer ID for the given string. It automatically adds the item to its\n  # internal mapping if it's not already present. For primitives defined in the DSL,\n  # they are expected to be known to the `Cookbook` instance.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent possesses at least one unit of the primitive, there's no need\n  # to collect more. Return an empty list as no actions are required.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Check if the primitive is a non-grabbable entity.\n  # According to the `CraftWorld` data attributes, `non_grabbable_indices`\n  # contains IDs of entities that cannot be picked up (e.g., water, workshops, boundaries).\n  # If the target primitive is non-grabbable, it cannot be 'collected' in the sense\n  # of adding it to inventory, so no actions should be returned.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Extract current state information required for pathfinding.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape  # Dimensions of the game grid.\n\n  # 5. Obtain integer mappings for movement and 'USE' actions from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']  # The action typically used to interact with or pick up items.\n\n  # Define the coordinate changes (delta_x, delta_y) for each movement action.\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # 6. Helper function to check if the `target_idx` (primitive) is in the 3x3\n  #    neighborhood around a given `check_pos` on the `current_grid`.\n  #    This mimics the `CraftState.next_to` method, which is the condition\n  #    for `ACTION_USE` to be effective for collection.\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Iterate through all 9 cells in the 3x3 square (including the center)\n    # around the `check_pos`.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # Check if the target primitive exists at this neighbor cell.\n          # `grid[nx, ny, target_idx]` returns the count of items of `target_idx` kind.\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True  # Target primitive found in the neighborhood.\n    return False  # Target primitive not found in the neighborhood.\n\n  # 7. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for shortest pathfinding.\n  # The queue `q` stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The `visited` set keeps track of grid positions already explored to prevent\n  # infinite loops (cycles) and redundant path computations, ensuring optimality.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS main loop: continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()  # Dequeue the next position and its path.\n\n    # If the current position is adjacent to (or on) the target primitive,\n    # we have found a valid point to perform the 'USE' action.\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the `ACTION_USE` to the path and return the complete sequence.\n      # This sequence represents the shortest path to collect the primitive.\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # If the primitive is not yet collectible from `curr_pos`, explore all\n    # possible valid moves from the current position.\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Validate the `next_pos`: ensure it is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue  # Skip moves that would take the agent out of bounds.\n\n      # If the `next_pos` has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      # This ensures the BFS processes the grid layer by layer, finding the shortest path first.\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)  # Mark the new position as visited.\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))  # Enqueue with the extended path.\n\n  # 8. If the BFS loop completes and the queue becomes empty, it means no path\n  #    was found from the `start_pos` to any cell adjacent to the target primitive.\n  #    In this case, the primitive is unreachable, and an empty list of actions is returned.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:37:08.349241", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive string is not known to the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Improvement for collect_v2: Check if the primitive is already in inventory.\n  # If the agent already has the item, no actions are needed to collect it.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # If the primitive is marked as non-grabbable in the world configuration,\n  # it cannot be 'collected' (picked up) in this manner, so no actions are returned.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state details\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for each action\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given position is next to (or on) the target primitive\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Check the 3x3 neighborhood around the current position\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor position is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # If the target primitive is found in this neighbor cell, return True\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n\n  # Initialize BFS queue with the starting position and an empty path\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) # (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_position)\n  # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is next to (or on) the primitive, we've found a path\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence of actions\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all possible moves from the current position\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # If the next position has not been visited, add it to the queue\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path is found (primitive is unreachable), return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:37:09.471467", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive string is not known to the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Improvement from collect_v1: If the primitive is non-grabbable, it cannot be collected into inventory.\n  # Return an empty list as no action sequence can achieve this.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Improvement for collect_v2: Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent already possesses the primitive, no further action is needed to \"collect\" it.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Already collected\n\n  # 2. Get current state details\n  # Note: current_state is already obtained above for the inventory check\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 3. Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for each action\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given position is next to (or on) the target primitive\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Check the 3x3 neighborhood around the current position\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]: # Including (0,0) for the current cell itself\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor position is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # If the target primitive is found in this neighbor cell (count > 0), return True\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n\n  # Initialize BFS queue with the starting position and an empty path\n  # Each element in the queue is (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_position)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is next to (or on) the primitive, we've found a path\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence of actions\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all possible moves from the current position\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # If the next position has not been visited, add it to the queue\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path is found (primitive is unreachable), return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:37:41.352086", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n  This function implements a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest\n  sequence of actions (movements and a final 'USE' action) required to collect\n  a specified primitive resource in the CraftWorld environment.\n\n  Improvements over `v1`:\n  - Removed unnecessary `try-except KeyError` block around `Index.index()` call,\n    as the `Index.index` method is designed to add new items if not present and\n    does not raise `KeyError` for valid string inputs (like the DSL primitives).\n  - Ensured all relevant checks (inventory, non-grabbable) are performed upfront\n    for early exit.\n  - Clearer structure and comments for each step of the collection logic.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation.\n      primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of action indices (integers) to execute in the environment.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is already collected,\n                 is non-grabbable, or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive string from the cookbook's index.\n  # The `Index.index()` method from the `Cookbook` class will always return an\n  # integer ID for the given string. It automatically adds the item to its\n  # internal mapping if it's not already present. For primitives defined in the DSL,\n  # they are expected to be known to the `Cookbook` instance, or will be added.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent possesses at least one unit of the primitive, there's no need\n  # to collect more. Return an empty list as no actions are required.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Check if the primitive is a non-grabbable entity.\n  # According to the `CraftWorld` data attributes, `non_grabbable_indices`\n  # contains IDs of entities that cannot be picked up (e.g., water, workshops, boundaries).\n  # If the target primitive is non-grabbable, it cannot be 'collected' in the sense\n  # of adding it to inventory, so no actions should be returned.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Extract current state information required for pathfinding.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape  # Dimensions of the game grid.\n\n  # 5. Obtain integer mappings for movement and 'USE' actions from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']  # The action typically used to interact with or pick up items.\n\n  # Define the coordinate changes (delta_x, delta_y) for each movement action.\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # 6. Helper function to check if the `target_idx` (primitive) is in the 3x3\n  #    neighborhood around a given `check_pos` on the `current_grid`.\n  #    This mimics the `CraftState.next_to` method, which is the condition\n  #    for `ACTION_USE` to be effective for collection.\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Iterate through all 9 cells in the 3x3 square (including the center)\n    # around the `check_pos`.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # Check if the target primitive exists at this neighbor cell.\n          # `grid[nx, ny, target_idx]` returns the count of items of `target_idx` kind.\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True  # Target primitive found in the neighborhood.\n    return False  # Target primitive not found in the neighborhood.\n\n  # 7. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for shortest pathfinding.\n  # The queue `q` stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The `visited` set keeps track of grid positions already explored to prevent\n  # infinite loops (cycles) and redundant path computations, ensuring optimality.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS main loop: continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()  # Dequeue the next position and its path.\n\n    # If the current position is adjacent to (or on) the target primitive,\n    # we have found a valid point to perform the 'USE' action.\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the `ACTION_USE` to the path and return the complete sequence.\n      # This sequence represents the shortest path to collect the primitive.\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # If the primitive is not yet collectible from `curr_pos`, explore all\n    # possible valid moves from the current position.\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Validate the `next_pos`: ensure it is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue  # Skip moves that would take the agent out of bounds.\n\n      # If the `next_pos` has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      # This ensures the BFS processes the grid layer by layer, finding the shortest path first.\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)  # Mark the new position as visited.\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))  # Enqueue with the extended path.\n\n  # 8. If the BFS loop completes and the queue becomes empty, it means no path\n  #    was found from the `start_pos` to any cell adjacent to the target primitive.\n  #    In this case, the primitive is unreachable, and an empty list of actions is returned.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:37:42.570859", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive string from the cookbook's index.\n  # The `Index.index()` method from the `Cookbook` class will always return an\n  # integer ID for the given string. It automatically adds the item to its\n  # internal mapping if it's not already present. For primitives defined in the DSL,\n  # they are expected to be known to the `Cookbook` instance.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent possesses at least one unit of the primitive, there's no need\n  # to collect more. Return an empty list as no actions are required.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Check if the primitive is a non-grabbable entity.\n  # According to the `CraftWorld` data attributes, `non_grabbable_indices`\n  # contains IDs of entities that cannot be picked up (e.g., water, workshops, boundaries).\n  # If the target primitive is non-grabbable, it cannot be 'collected' in the sense\n  # of adding it to inventory, so no actions should be returned.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Extract current state information required for pathfinding.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape  # Dimensions of the game grid.\n\n  # 5. Obtain integer mappings for movement and 'USE' actions from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']  # The action typically used to interact with or pick up items.\n\n  # Define the coordinate changes (delta_x, delta_y) for each movement action.\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # 6. Helper function to check if the `target_idx` (primitive) is in the 3x3\n  #    neighborhood around a given `check_pos` on the `current_grid`.\n  #    This mimics the `CraftState.next_to` method, which is the condition\n  #    for `ACTION_USE` to be effective for collection.\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Iterate through all 9 cells in the 3x3 square (including the center)\n    # around the `check_pos`.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # Check if the target primitive exists at this neighbor cell.\n          # `grid[nx, ny, target_idx]` returns the count of items of `target_idx` kind.\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True  # Target primitive found in the neighborhood.\n    return False  # Target primitive not found in the neighborhood.\n\n  # 7. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for shortest pathfinding.\n  # The queue `q` stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The `visited` set keeps track of grid positions already explored to prevent\n  # infinite loops (cycles) and redundant path computations, ensuring optimality.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS main loop: continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()  # Dequeue the next position and its path.\n\n    # If the current position is adjacent to (or on) the target primitive,\n    # we have found a valid point to perform the 'USE' action.\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the `ACTION_USE` to the path and return the complete sequence.\n      # This sequence represents the shortest path to collect the primitive.\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # If the primitive is not yet collectible from `curr_pos`, explore all\n    # possible valid moves from the current position.\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Validate the `next_pos`: ensure it is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue  # Skip moves that would take the agent out of bounds.\n\n      # If the `next_pos` has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      # This ensures the BFS processes the grid layer by layer, finding the shortest path first.\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)  # Mark the new position as visited.\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))  # Enqueue with the extended path.\n\n  # 8. If the BFS loop completes and the queue becomes empty, it means no path\n  #    was found from the `start_pos` to any cell adjacent to the target primitive.\n  #    In this case, the primitive is unreachable, and an empty list of actions is returned.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:38:28.641646", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by checking inventory first.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Resolve the primitive name to its corresponding integer index.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized by the environment's index,\n      # it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Retrieve the current state of the environment.\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # 3. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  #    If it is, no actions are needed to collect it.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Crucial check: Verify if the primitive is designed to be 'grabbable'.\n  #    Only grabbable items can be directly added to the inventory via collection.\n  #    For example, 'WOOD' (trees) might not be grabbable, but 'PLANK' (produced from trees) is.\n  #    This function aims to put the `primitive` itself into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      # If the item cannot be picked up or directly put into inventory using 'USE' action,\n      # this `collect` function is not applicable for it.\n      return []\n\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) grid coordinates.\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # 5. Obtain the integer action mappings for movement and 'USE' from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # (dx, dy) for moving down.\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # (dx, dy) for moving up.\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving left.\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving right.\n  ]\n\n  # 6. Identify all grid cells where the target primitive is located.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0: # Check if the cell contains any amount of the primitive.\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not present anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 7. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  #    The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  # Keep track of visited positions to prevent infinite loops in cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {agent_pos} \n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to (or on top of) any primitive location.\n      # The 'USE' action typically operates on a 3x3 neighborhood around the agent.\n      # This matches the behavior of CraftState.next_to(i_kind).\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent cell is found, append the 'USE' action and return the full path.\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the valid grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the next cell is traversable or an impassable obstacle.\n          # A cell is impassable if it contains a non-grabbable entity that is\n          # neither a workshop nor water (which are typically traversable points of interaction).\n          is_impassable = False\n          for k_idx in range(num_kinds): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # Check if any item kind is present at the cell.\n                  if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and\\\n                     k_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices and\\\n                     k_idx != env.world.water_index:\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # Found an impassable obstacle; no need to check further kinds in this cell.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path; the cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:38:29.824055", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`. Refines obstacle definition for clarity and robustness.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Resolve the primitive name to its corresponding integer index.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized by the environment's index,\n      # it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Crucial check: Verify if the primitive is designed to be 'grabbable'.\n  #    Only grabbable items can be directly added to the inventory via collection.\n  #    This function aims to put the `primitive` itself into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      # If the item cannot be picked up or directly put into inventory using 'USE' action,\n      # this `collect` function is not applicable for it.\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Retrieve the current state of the environment.\n  state = env._current_state\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) grid coordinates.\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # 4. Obtain the integer action mappings for movement and 'USE' from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # (dx, dy) for moving down.\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # (dx, dy) for moving up.\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving left.\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving right.\n  ]\n\n  # 5. Identify all grid cells where the target primitive is located.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0: # Check if the cell contains any amount of the primitive.\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not present anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Pre-calculate the set of indices that represent impassable terrain.\n  # These are non-grabbable entities that are NOT workshops and NOT water.\n  # Using sets for efficient lookups.\n  impassable_kinds = env.world.non_grabbable_indices.copy()\n  impassable_kinds.difference_update(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  # Ensure water is also not considered impassable if it's in non_grabbable_indices\n  if env.world.water_index in impassable_kinds:\n      impassable_kinds.remove(env.world.water_index)\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  #    The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  # Keep track of visited positions to prevent infinite loops in cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {agent_pos} \n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to (or on top of) any primitive location.\n      # The 'USE' action typically operates on a 3x3 neighborhood around the agent.\n      # This matches the behavior of CraftState.next_to(i_kind).\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent cell is found, append the 'USE' action and return the full path.\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the valid grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the next cell is traversable or an impassable obstacle.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Iterate through all kinds present at the next cell\n          for k_idx in range(num_kinds): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # Check if any item kind is present at the cell.\n                  if k_idx in impassable_kinds: # Use the pre-calculated set for efficiency and clarity.\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # Found an impassable obstacle; no need to check further kinds in this cell.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path; the cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:39:31.967227", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Finds the shortest path to a primitive and returns actions to collect it.\n\n    This function utilizes Breadth-First Search (BFS) to determine the shortest\n    sequence of movement actions required to reach a position from which the target\n    primitive can be collected, followed by a 'USE' action.\n\n    The pathfinding algorithm carefully considers environmental obstacles:\n    - The agent can move onto cells containing the target primitive itself.\n    - Other grabbable items (not the target primitive) are also traversable.\n    - Specific non-grabbable entities like workshops and water are traversable.\n    - All other non-grabbable entities (e.g., boundary walls, solid blocks not\n      meant for collection) are treated as impassable barriers.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance, providing access\n                            to the current game state, grid layout, and item indices.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of integer action IDs (from `env.action_specs()`)\n                   representing the shortest path to collect the primitive,\n                   including the final 'USE' action. Returns an empty list if\n                   the primitive is not found on the map or is unreachable from\n                   the agent's current position.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Resolve the primitive's string name to its unique integer ID.\n  # The `cookbook.index` maps item names to their integer IDs.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized by the environment,\n      # it cannot be collected. Return an empty action list.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract current state information from the environment.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  agent_pos = current_state.pos  # The agent's current (x, y) coordinates.\n  grid = current_state.grid      # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Dimensions for boundary checks.\n\n  # 3. Obtain the integer mappings for movement and interaction actions.\n  # These are necessary to construct the action sequence.\n  action_ids = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_ids['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_ids['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_ids['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_ids['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_ids['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements as (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # This facilitates exploring neighboring cells during the BFS.\n  move_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move one unit in the positive Y direction.\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move one unit in the negative Y direction.\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move one unit in the negative X direction.\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move one unit in the positive X direction.\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Pre-locate all instances of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # This list helps optimize the goal check during BFS by providing specific\n  # target points to check proximity against.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # A primitive is considered present if its count at (x, y) is greater than 0.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map,\n      # there's nothing to collect. Return an empty path.\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x, y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of positions already explored to prevent cycles\n  # and redundant path computations, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited = {agent_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path_to_current = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is within the effective range for the 'USE' action.\n      # The 'USE' action allows collecting items within a 3x3 square centered on the\n      # primitive's location (i.e., agent is adjacent or on top of the primitive).\n      can_use_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # A position (cx, cy) is within 3x3 range of (px, py) if the maximum\n          # absolute difference in coordinates is 1 or less.\n          if max(abs(cx - px), abs(cy - py)) <= 1:\n              can_use_primitive = True\n              break # Found a primitive within 'USE' range, no need to check others.\n      \n      if can_use_primitive:\n          # If a position from which the primitive can be 'USED' is found,\n          # append the 'USE' action to the path and return the complete sequence.\n          path_to_current.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path_to_current\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighboring cells from the current position.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # First, ensure the prospective next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n          # Second, determine if the next cell is traversable.\n          # A cell is considered impassable if it contains certain non-grabbable entities\n          # that act as physical obstacles.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Iterate through all 'kinds' (entity types) that might be present at `next_pos`.\n          for k_idx in range(grid.shape[2]):\n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If an entity of kind `k_idx` is present.\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx:\n                      # If the cell contains the target primitive itself, the agent CAN move onto it.\n                      pass # This is not an obstacle for movement.\n                  elif k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                      # For other non-grabbable entities:\n                      # Workshops and water are special non-grabbable entities that are\n                      # traversable and often serve as interaction points.\n                      if k_idx in env.world.workshop_indices or k_idx == env.world.water_index:\n                          pass # Allow movement onto these specific non-grabbable types.\n                      else:\n                          # Any other non-grabbable entity (e.g., 'BOUNDARY' walls, solid\n                          # rock if not the target primitive) is considered a physical obstacle.\n                          is_impassable = True\n                          break # This cell is impassable; no need to check other kinds.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip adding this path if the next cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet in this BFS,\n          # add it to the queue for further exploration.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new path list by extending the current path to avoid modifying\n              # shared lists among different BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path_to_current)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to a collectable position was found,\n  # it implies the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:39:33.116751", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"This function finds the shortest path for the agent to reach and collect\n    a specified primitive item in the CraftLab environment. It uses Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n    to navigate the grid, considering obstacles and valid interaction ranges.\n\n    The strategy involves:\n    1. Identifying the integer ID for the target primitive.\n    2. Locating all instances of the primitive on the grid.\n    3. Performing a BFS from the agent's current position to find the shortest\n       sequence of movement actions that lead to a cell from which the 'USE'\n       action can successfully collect the primitive.\n    4. Appending a 'USE' action to the found path.\n\n    Obstacles: The BFS considers certain non-grabbable entities (e.g., 'BOUNDARY')\n    as impassable, while others (e.g., 'WORKSHOP', 'WATER') are traversable\n    interaction points. The primitive itself is traversable for movement but is\n    the target for the 'USE' action.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list of integer action IDs representing the shortest path\n                   to collect the primitive, ending with a 'USE' action.\n                   Returns an empty list if the primitive is not found or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid position is impassable for movement.\n  def _is_position_impassable(x: int, y: int, grid: np.ndarray, world_config: craft.CraftWorld, target_primitive_idx: int) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if a given grid position (x, y) is traversable by the agent.\n      \n      Args:\n          x (int): The x-coordinate of the position to check.\n          y (int): The y-coordinate of the position to check.\n          grid (np.ndarray): The current grid state.\n          world_config (craft.CraftWorld): The world configuration for obstacle definitions.\n          target_primitive_idx (int): The index of the primitive being collected.\n      \n      Returns:\n          bool: True if the position is impassable, False otherwise.\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n      # 1. Check if the position is out of grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return True # Out of bounds is always impassable.\n\n      # 2. Check entities present at the position for impassability.\n      # Iterate through all 'kinds' (layers) at the given cell.\n      # If any kind at this cell makes it impassable, the cell is impassable.\n      for k_idx in range(num_kinds):\n          if grid[x, y, k_idx] > 0: # If something of kind `k_idx` is present at (x, y)\n              # The target primitive itself is always traversable for movement.\n              if k_idx == target_primitive_idx:\n                  continue\n              \n              # Check if it's a non-grabbable entity.\n              if k_idx in world_config.non_grabbable_indices:\n                  # Special non-grabbable entities like workshops and water are traversable.\n                  if k_idx in world_config.workshop_indices or k_idx == world_config.water_index:\n                      continue\n                  else:\n                      # Any other non-grabbable entity (e.g., 'BOUNDARY') is an obstacle.\n                      return True\n      return False # No impassable entity found at this position.\n\n\n  # 1. Resolve the primitive's string name to its unique integer ID.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      return [] # Primitive name not recognized.\n\n  # 2. Extract crucial information from the current environment state.\n  state = env._current_state\n  initial_pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  world_config = env.world # Reference to CraftWorld instance for obstacle checks\n\n  # 3. Obtain the integer mappings for movement and interaction actions.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # (dx, dy) for moving down, action_id\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # (dx, dy) for moving up, action_id\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving left, action_id\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving right, action_id\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  # This list helps in determining potential targets for collection.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # A primitive is considered present if its count at (x, y) is greater than 0.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return [] # No instances of the primitive found on the map.\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x, y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])])\n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of positions already explored to prevent cycles.\n  visited = {initial_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is within the effective range for the 'USE' action.\n      # The 'USE' action can collect items in a 3x3 square centered on the primitive's location.\n      is_within_use_range = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # A position is within 'USE' range if its maximum coordinate difference\n          # to the primitive's location is 1 (i.e., adjacent or on the same spot).\n          if max(abs(cx - px), abs(cy - py)) <= 1:\n              is_within_use_range = True\n              break # Found a primitive within 'USE' range.\n      \n      if is_within_use_range:\n          # If a position from which the primitive can be 'USED' is found,\n          # append the 'USE' action and return the complete path.\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells from the current position.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Use the helper function to determine if the next position is impassable.\n          # This handles both out-of-bounds and obstacle checks.\n          if _is_position_impassable(next_x, next_y, grid, world_config, primitive_idx):\n              continue # Skip this next position if it's an obstacle or out of bounds.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              new_path = list(path) # Create a new path list for this branch.\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to a collectable position was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:40:35.784181", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # The requested primitive name is not recognized by the environment's cookbook.\n      return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  state = env._current_state\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      # If the agent already has at least one of the primitive, no collection actions are needed.\n      return []\n\n  # The 'collect' function implies obtaining the item in inventory.\n  # If the primitive is not in the set of items that can be picked up (grabbable),\n  # it cannot be \"collected\" in the sense of adding to inventory directly.\n  # For example, 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER', 'WORKSHOP0' are not meant to be picked up.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve current state information from the environment.\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid.\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer action mappings from the environment for movement and 'USE'.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # (dx, dy) for moving down.\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # (dx, dy) for moving up.\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving left.\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving right.\n  ]\n\n  # Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  # Using numpy's where for a potentially more efficient way to find locations.\n  # np.where returns a tuple of arrays, one for each dimension. We zip them together.\n  primitive_locations = list(zip(*np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] > 0)))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Pre-compute the set of non-grabbable entities that are still traversable.\n  # These typically include workshops and water, which the agent can move through.\n  traversable_non_grabbables = set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  traversable_non_grabbables.add(env.world.water_index)\n\n  # Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any cell that is adjacent to the target primitive.\n  # The queue stores (current_position, path_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant computations.\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to (or on the same cell as)\n      # any of the primitive's known locations. A 3x3 neighborhood is considered\n      # \"adjacent\" for the purpose of the 'USE' action in CraftWorld.\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent cell is found, append the 'USE' action and return\n          # the complete sequence of actions (movement + use).\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Refined check for impassable cells:\n          # A cell is impassable if any entity present in it is non-grabbable\n          # AND that non-grabbable entity is not designated as traversable (like workshops/water).\n          \n          # Get all kinds present at the next cell. np.where returns (array_of_indices,).\n          present_kinds_at_next_pos = np.where(grid[next_x, next_y, :] > 0)[0]\n\n          is_impassable = False\n          for k_idx in present_kinds_at_next_pos:\n              if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and \\\n                 k_idx not in traversable_non_grabbables:\n                  is_impassable = True\n                  break # Found an impassable entity, no need to check further for this cell.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path if the cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Using path + [action_id] creates a new list, which is good practice for BFS.\n              queue.append((next_pos, path + [action_id]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive is found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:40:36.947372", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\"\"\"\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # The requested primitive name is not recognized by the environment's cookbook.\n      return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  state = env._current_state\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      # If the agent already has at least one of the primitive, no collection actions are needed.\n      return []\n\n  # The 'collect' function implies obtaining the item into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is not in the set of items that can be picked up (grabbable),\n  # it cannot be \"collected\" in the sense of adding to inventory directly.\n  # For example, 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER', 'WORKSHOP0' are environmental features not meant to be picked up.\n  # Note: `env.world.grabbable_indices` is a list, so membership check is O(N).\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve current state information from the environment.\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid.\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer action mappings from the environment for movement and 'USE'.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # (dx, dy) for moving down.\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # (dx, dy) for moving up.\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving left.\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving right.\n  ]\n\n  # Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # If the cell contains at least one unit of the target primitive.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Pre-compute the set of non-grabbable entities that are still traversable.\n  # These typically include workshops and water, which the agent can move through.\n  traversable_non_grabbables = set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  traversable_non_grabbables.add(env.world.water_index)\n\n  # Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any cell from which the 'USE' action can successfully\n  # interact with the primitive. This means any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # (including the center) of a primitive's actual location, as per CraftState.next_to.\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])]) # Stores (current_position, path_taken_to_reach_here).\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant computations.\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to (or on the same cell as)\n      # any of the primitive's known locations. A 3x3 neighborhood is considered\n      # \"adjacent\" for the purpose of the 'USE' action in CraftWorld.\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent cell is found, append the 'USE' action and return\n          # the complete sequence of actions (movement + use).\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the next cell is traversable or an impassable obstacle.\n          # A cell is considered impassable if it contains any non-grabbable entity\n          # that is NOT in the set of traversable non-grabbables.\n          is_impassable = False\n          for k_idx in range(num_kinds): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If there's something of kind k_idx at this cell...\n                  if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and\\\n                     k_idx not in traversable_non_grabbables:\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # No need to check other kinds in this cell; it's blocked.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path if the cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive is found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position given the current grid.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:41:24.409410", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by pre-calculating impassable entity kinds for clearer and potentially more efficient obstacle checking during pathfinding.\n\n    This function uses Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence of\n    movement actions to reach a position from which the target primitive can be\n    collected using the 'USE' action.\n\n    A 'USE' action is effective if the agent is within a 3x3 square centered\n    on the target primitive's location (i.e., on the same cell or one cell away\n    orthogonally or diagonally).\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list of action integers (from `env.action_specs()`) representing\n                   the shortest path to collect the primitive. Returns an empty list\n                   if the primitive is not found in the environment or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Map the primitive name to its integer index using the environment's cookbook.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name does not correspond to a known item, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract necessary state information from the current environment state.\n  state = env._current_state\n  initial_pos = state.pos  # Agent's starting (x, y) coordinates\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 3. Get the integer action IDs from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs for BFS exploration.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move one cell down (increase y)\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move one cell up (decrease y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move one cell left (decrease x)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move one cell right (increase x)\n  ]\n\n  # Pre-calculate the set of entity kinds that truly act as impassable obstacles.\n  # These are non-grabbable entities that are NOT workshops and NOT water,\n  # meaning the agent cannot move onto them.\n  true_impassable_kinds = (\n      set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) -\n      set(env.world.workshop_indices) -\n      {env.world.water_index}\n  )\n\n  # 4. Find all locations on the grid where the target primitive currently exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # Check if the primitive kind's layer at (x, y) has a non-zero count.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map, no collection is possible.\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])])\n  # The visited set stores positions (x,y) to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {initial_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is within the 'USE' range of any primitive location.\n      # The 'USE' action works if the agent is in the 3x3 neighborhood (including the cell itself).\n      is_within_use_range = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # Calculate Chebyshev distance (max of dx, dy) for 3x3 neighborhood check.\n          if max(abs(cx - px), abs(cy - py)) <= 1:\n              is_within_use_range = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_within_use_range:\n          # If a suitable position is found, append the 'USE' action and return the complete path.\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells from the current position.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # First, check if the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds\n\n          # Second, determine if the next cell is traversable.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Iterate through all possible kinds/layers at the next cell.\n          for k_idx in range(grid.shape[2]): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If something of kind `k_idx` is present at this cell.\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx:\n                      # Agent can move onto the primitive itself to collect it. It is traversable.\n                      continue \n                  # Check if the present kind is one of the pre-computed true obstacles.\n                  if k_idx in true_impassable_kinds:\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # Found an obstacle, no need to check further kinds in this cell.\n\n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this next position if it's blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new path list by extending the current path.\n              new_path = list(path)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:41:25.622654", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` with a more explicit and robust obstacle definition.\n\n    This function refines the obstacle detection logic within the Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n    to clearly distinguish between traversable and impassable grid cells. It computes a\n    definitive set of \"hard obstacles\" (entities that absolutely block movement) to ensure\n    that the agent only plans paths through navigable terrain.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list of action integers (from `env.action_specs()`) representing\n                   the shortest path to collect the primitive. Returns an empty list\n                   if the primitive is not found in the environment or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Map the primitive name to its integer index using the environment's cookbook.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name does not correspond to a known item, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract necessary state information from the current environment state.\n  state = env._current_state\n  initial_pos = state.pos  # Agent's starting (x, y) coordinates\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 3. Get the integer action IDs from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs for BFS exploration.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move one cell down (increase y)\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move one cell up (decrease y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move one cell left (decrease x)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move one cell right (increase x)\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Find all locations on the grid where the target primitive currently exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # Check if the primitive kind's layer at (x, y) has a non-zero count.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map, no collection is possible.\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Define \"hard obstacles\": these are non-grabbable entities that completely block movement.\n  # We start with all non-grabbable indices.\n  hard_obstacle_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # Remove entities that are non-grabbable but are still traversable (e.g., workshops, water).\n  hard_obstacle_indices -= set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  hard_obstacle_indices -= {env.world.water_index}\n\n  # Crucially, remove the primitive itself from the list of hard obstacles.\n  # The agent needs to be able to move onto (or adjacent to) the primitive to collect it.\n  if primitive_idx in hard_obstacle_indices:\n      hard_obstacle_indices.remove(primitive_idx)\n\n  # 6. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])])\n  # The visited set stores positions (x,y) to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {initial_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is within the 'USE' range of any primitive location.\n      # The 'USE' action works if the agent is in the 3x3 neighborhood (including the cell itself).\n      is_within_use_range = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # Calculate Chebyshev distance (max of dx, dy) for 3x3 neighborhood check.\n          if max(abs(cx - px), abs(cy - py)) <= 1:\n              is_within_use_range = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_within_use_range:\n          # If a suitable position is found, append the 'USE' action and return the complete path.\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells from the current position.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # First, check if the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds\n\n          # Second, determine if the next cell is traversable using the pre-defined hard obstacles.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Iterate through the specific hard obstacle indices.\n          for k_idx in hard_obstacle_indices:\n              # If any hard obstacle kind is present at the next cell, it's impassable.\n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_impassable = True\n                  break \n\n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this next position if it's blocked by a hard obstacle.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new path list by extending the current path.\n              new_path = list(path)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:42:41.998190", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  # The Index class's __getitem__ method returns int or None.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             primitive_idx == cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, we have found the shortest path.\n    # This is because BFS explores layer by layer, guaranteeing that the first time\n    # a goal condition is met for a dequeued state, its path is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      # Return the combined path immediately\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        if new_pos not in visited:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If the queue becomes empty and no goal was reached, the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:42:43.225357", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define internal direction mappings for CraftState\n  # Assuming DMLab-style direction encoding: 0=N (Up), 1=E (Right), 2=S (Down), 3=W (Left)\n  DIR_UP = 0\n  DIR_RIGHT = 1\n  DIR_DOWN = 2\n  DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy), their corresponding action ID, and resulting direction\n  MOVES_WITH_DIR = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP, DIR_UP),      # Move Up (y-1), agent faces Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN, DIR_DOWN),   # Move Down (y+1), agent faces Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT, DIR_LEFT),  # Move Left (x-1), agent faces Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT, DIR_RIGHT), # Move Right (x+1), agent faces Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position and initial direction\n  start_pos = state.pos\n  start_dir = state.dir # Agent's starting direction\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             primitive_idx == cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n\n  # Case 1: Primitive is a \"reach-and-be-on\" type (workshop, water, stone, boundary)\n  # For these, we only need to find the shortest path to a cell containing the primitive.\n  # No 'USE' action is involved, and direction doesn't matter for collection.\n  if is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n    q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) # (current_position, list_of_actions)\n    visited = {start_pos} # Set of visited positions\n\n    while q:\n      current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if current_pos contains the target primitive\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        return current_actions # Found the shortest path, return immediately\n\n      # Explore neighbors\n      for dx, dy, action, _ in MOVES_WITH_DIR: # _ for unused direction\n        new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n        new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n        # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries and not visited\n        if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n          if new_pos not in visited:\n            visited.add(new_pos)\n            q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n    \n    return [] # No path found to the primitive\n\n  # Case 2: Primitive is a \"grabbable\" type (e.g., WOOD, IRON, GRASS)\n  # These require an ACTION_USE, and the 'USE' action depends on the agent's current direction.\n  # Thus, the BFS state must include direction.\n  elif is_grabbable:\n    # BFS state: (current_position, current_direction, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n    q = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])]) \n    visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)} # Set of visited (position, direction) tuples\n\n    min_path_len = float('inf')\n    best_path_actions = []\n\n    while q:\n      current_pos, current_dir, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # Determine the cell \"in front\" of the agent based on current_dir\n      target_x, target_y = current_pos[0], current_pos[1]\n      if current_dir == DIR_UP:\n        target_y -= 1\n      elif current_dir == DIR_DOWN:\n        target_y += 1\n      elif current_dir == DIR_LEFT:\n        target_x -= 1\n      elif current_dir == DIR_RIGHT:\n        target_x += 1\n      \n      # Check if the cell \"in front\" is valid and contains the primitive\n      if (0 <= target_x < WIDTH and 0 <= target_y < HEIGHT and \n          grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n        \n        total_actions = current_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n        if len(total_actions) < min_path_len:\n          min_path_len = len(total_actions)\n          best_path_actions = total_actions\n        # Do NOT break here. BFS finds shortest path to (pos, dir) states.\n        # However, a slightly longer path to a (pos, dir) state might lead to a shorter\n        # *total* sequence if it allows a 'USE' action that's quicker overall.\n        # We need to explore all possibilities to find the true shortest path including USE.\n\n      # Explore neighbors (movement actions also change direction)\n      for dx, dy, action, new_dir in MOVES_WITH_DIR:\n        new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n        new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n        # Check if the new (position, direction) state is valid and not visited\n        if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n          if (new_pos, new_dir) not in visited:\n            visited.add((new_pos, new_dir))\n            q.append((new_pos, new_dir, current_actions + [action]))\n    \n    return best_path_actions # Return the shortest path found\n\n  # If the primitive is neither grabbable, nor workshop, nor stationary, it's uncollectible by this function.\n  else:\n    return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:43:04.696714", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Get the current state of the environment\n  state = env._current_state\n  actions = []\n\n  # 3. Check if the agent is already adjacent to the primitive\n  # If so, just perform the USE action to collect/interact with it\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n    return actions\n\n  # 4. Initialize grid dimensions and agent position\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the set of non-grabbable (obstacle) indices for pathfinding\n  obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # 5. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      # Check if this cell contains the primitive\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, return an empty list\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any cell that is adjacent to any instance of the primitive,\n  #    while avoiding obstacles.\n  #    Queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_actions_so_far)\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  best_path_to_adjacent = None\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding action indices\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), env.action_specs()['DOWN']),\n      ((0, -1), env.action_specs()['UP']),\n      ((1, 0), env.action_specs()['RIGHT']),\n      ((-1, 0), env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos, path = q.popleft()\n    curr_x, curr_y = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive locations\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_locations:\n      # Manhattan distance of 1 means it's adjacent\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) + abs(curr_y - target_y) == 1:\n        best_path_to_adjacent = path\n        break  # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n    \n    if best_path_to_adjacent:\n      break  # Path found, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for (dx, dy), action_idx in moves:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if the next position is blocked by an obstacle\n      is_blocked = False\n      for obstacle_idx in obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_blocked = True\n          break\n      \n      if is_blocked:\n        continue # Cannot move to a blocked cell\n\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        new_path = path + [action_idx]\n        q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # 7. If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the USE action\n  if best_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n    actions.extend(best_path_to_adjacent)\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:43:05.819656", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Get the current state of the environment\n  state = env._current_state\n  actions = []\n\n  # 3. Check if the agent is already adjacent to the primitive\n  # If so, just perform the USE action to collect/interact with it\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n    return actions\n\n  # 4. Initialize grid dimensions and agent position\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = grid.shape # N_KINDS is needed for obstacle check\n\n  # Get the set of non-grabbable indices from the world\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # 5. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      # Check if this cell contains the primitive\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, return an empty list\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any cell that is adjacent to any instance of the primitive.\n  #    Queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_actions_so_far)\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  best_path_to_adjacent = None\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding action indices\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), env.action_specs()['DOWN']),\n      ((0, -1), env.action_specs()['UP']),\n      ((1, 0), env.action_specs()['RIGHT']),\n      ((-1, 0), env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos, path = q.popleft()\n    curr_x, curr_y = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive locations\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_locations:\n      # Manhattan distance of 1 means it's adjacent\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) + abs(curr_y - target_y) == 1:\n        best_path_to_adjacent = path\n        break  # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n    \n    if best_path_to_adjacent:\n      break  # Path found, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for (dx, dy), action_idx in moves:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # --- IMPROVEMENT FOR V2: Check for obstacles (non-grabbable items) ---\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for k in range(N_KINDS):\n          # If the cell contains an item that is non-grabbable and agent cannot move into it\n          # Note: This assumes non_grabbable_indices correctly identifies impassable terrain.\n          if grid[next_x, next_y, k] > 0 and k in non_grabbable_indices:\n              is_obstacle = True\n              break\n      if is_obstacle:\n          continue # Skip this path, as it leads to an impassable cell\n\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        new_path = path + [action_idx]\n        q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # 7. If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the USE action\n  if best_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n    actions.extend(best_path_to_adjacent)\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:43:59.726509", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  # If the primitive name is not valid or not found, return an empty list of actions.\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    return []\n\n  # Optimization: If the agent already possesses the primitive in its inventory,\n  # no collection actions are needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Retrieve the integer mappings for movement and interaction actions.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # A dictionary to map (delta_x, delta_y) movements to their corresponding action integers.\n  dir_to_action = {\n      (0, -1): UP,   # Move Up (decreasing Y)\n      (0, 1): DOWN,  # Move Down (increasing Y)\n      (-1, 0): LEFT, # Move Left (decreasing X)\n      (1, 0): RIGHT, # Move Right (increasing X)\n  }\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 3. Identify indices of entities that block agent movement (impassable terrain).\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  # Safely get indices for common impassable items\n  boundary_idx = cookbook.index.get('BOUNDARY')\n  water_idx = cookbook.index.get('WATER')\n  if boundary_idx is not None:\n      impassable_indices.add(boundary_idx)\n  if water_idx is not None:\n      impassable_indices.add(water_idx)\n\n  # 4. Helper function to determine if a given grid cell is traversable.\n  def is_cell_traversable(x, y):\n      # Check if coordinates are within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False\n      # Check if the cell contains any impassable entity.\n      for imp_idx in impassable_indices:\n          if grid[x, y, imp_idx] == 1:\n              return False\n      return True\n\n  # Initial check: If the agent's current position is not traversable, it cannot move.\n  if not is_cell_traversable(agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1]):\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Find all grid locations where the desired primitive currently exists.\n  primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, return an empty list of actions.\n  if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Determine the set of valid 'target cells' for the BFS.\n  # These are traversable locations from which the agent can successfully 'USE' the primitive\n  # (i.e., any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood of a primitive).\n  bfs_target_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive's location.\n    for dx_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx_n, py + dy_n\n        \n        # If this neighboring cell is traversable, it's a potential target for the agent.\n        if is_cell_traversable(nx, ny):\n          bfs_target_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # If no traversable cells are found around any primitive, no path can be found.\n  if not bfs_target_cells:\n      return []\n\n  # 7. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the `bfs_target_cells`.\n  q = collections.deque([agent_pos])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Set to keep track of visited coordinates to prevent cycles.\n  parent = {agent_pos: None} # Dictionary to reconstruct the path: {child_pos: parent_pos}.\n\n  target_found_pos = None # Stores the specific target cell that was reached first.\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos = q.popleft()\n    \n    # If the current position is one of our target cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if current_pos in bfs_target_cells:\n      target_found_pos = current_pos\n      break # Stop BFS as the shortest path to a target has been found.\n\n    # Explore the four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n    for dx, dy in [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]:\n      next_x, next_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is valid (within bounds, traversable, and not visited).\n      if is_cell_traversable(next_x, next_y) and next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        parent[next_pos] = current_pos # Store parent for path reconstruction.\n        q.append(next_pos)\n  \n  # 8. Path reconstruction.\n  if target_found_pos is None:\n    # If the queue became empty and no path to any target cell was found,\n    # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n    return []\n  \n  path_actions = []\n  current = target_found_pos\n  while parent[current] is not None:\n    prev = parent[current]\n    dx, dy = current[0] - prev[0], current[1] - prev[1]\n    # Convert (dx, dy) to an action (e.g., (0, -1) -> UP).\n    path_actions.append(dir_to_action[(dx, dy)])\n    current = prev\n  \n  path_actions.reverse() # The path is built in reverse, so reverse it to get the correct order.\n  \n  # 9. Append the 'USE' action and return the complete sequence.\n  return path_actions + [USE]", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:44:00.880343", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by adding an inventory check and refining comments.\"\"\"\n  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) coordinates\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  #    If the primitive name is not valid or not found, return an empty list of actions.\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Optimization: Check if the agent already possesses the primitive in its inventory.\n  #    If so, no collection actions are needed, as the primitive is already \"collected\".\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Retrieve the integer mappings for movement and interaction actions.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 4. A dictionary to map (delta_x, delta_y) movements to their corresponding action integers.\n  #    This is crucial for reconstructing the path from BFS results.\n  dir_to_action = {\n      (0, -1): UP,   # Move Up (decreasing Y coordinate)\n      (0, 1): DOWN,  # Move Down (increasing Y coordinate)\n      (-1, 0): LEFT, # Move Left (decreasing X coordinate)\n      (1, 0): RIGHT, # Move Right (increasing X coordinate)\n  }\n\n  # 5. Get grid dimensions.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 6. Identify indices of entities that block agent movement (impassable terrain).\n  #    Based on typical CraftWorld setups, 'BOUNDARY' and 'WATER' are common impassable blocks.\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_indices.add(cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  if 'WATER' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_indices.add(cookbook.index['WATER'])\n\n  # 7. Helper function to determine if a given grid cell is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_cell_traversable(x, y):\n      # Check if the coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False  # Cell is out of bounds.\n\n      # Check if the cell contains any impassable entity.\n      for imp_idx in impassable_indices:\n          if grid[x, y, imp_idx] == 1:\n              return False  # Cell is blocked by an impassable object.\n      return True\n\n  # 8. Initial check: If the agent's current position is not traversable, it cannot move.\n  if not is_cell_traversable(agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1]):\n      return []\n\n  # 9. Find all grid locations where the desired primitive currently exists.\n  primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n\n  # 10. If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, return an empty list of actions.\n  if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 11. Determine the set of valid 'target cells' for the BFS.\n  #     A target cell is any traversable location from which the agent can successfully\n  #     'USE' the primitive. The `CraftState.next_to` method implies the 'USE' action\n  #     works for any primitive within a 3x3 neighborhood (including the agent's cell).\n  bfs_target_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive's location.\n    for dx_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx_n, py + dy_n\n        \n        # If this neighboring cell is traversable, it's a potential target for the agent.\n        if is_cell_traversable(nx, ny):\n          bfs_target_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # 12. If no traversable cells are found around any primitive (e.g., all primitives are\n  #     surrounded by impassable terrain), no path can be found.\n  if not bfs_target_cells:\n      return []\n\n  # 13. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #     from the agent's current position to any of the `bfs_target_cells`.\n  #     The queue stores (current_x, current_y) tuples.\n  q = collections.deque([agent_pos])\n  # `visited` set tracks cells (coordinates) that have already been added to the queue\n  # to prevent cycles and redundant paths, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited = {agent_pos}\n  # `parent` dictionary to reconstruct the path: {child_pos: parent_pos}.\n  parent = {agent_pos: None} \n\n  target_found_pos = None # Will store the first target cell found by BFS\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos = q.popleft()\n    \n    # If the current position is one of our target cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if current_pos in bfs_target_cells:\n      target_found_pos = current_pos\n      break # Stop BFS as the shortest path to a target has been found.\n\n    # Explore the four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n    for dx, dy in [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]: # (dx, dy) for Up, Down, Left, Right respectively\n      next_x, next_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is valid (within grid boundaries, traversable, and not visited).\n      if is_cell_traversable(next_x, next_y) and next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos) # Mark as visited.\n        parent[next_pos] = current_pos # Store current as parent of next for path reconstruction.\n        q.append(next_pos) # Add the new state to the queue.\n  \n  # 14. Path reconstruction.\n  if target_found_pos is None:\n    # If the queue became empty and no path to any target cell was found,\n    # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n    return []\n  \n  path_to_target = []\n  current = target_found_pos\n  # Reconstruct path by backtracking from the target to the agent's start position using parent pointers.\n  while parent[current] is not None:\n    prev = parent[current]\n    dx, dy = current[0] - prev[0], current[1] - prev[1]\n    # Convert the (dx, dy) movement to its corresponding action integer.\n    path_to_target.append(dir_to_action[(dx, dy)])\n    current = prev\n  \n  path_to_target.reverse() # The path was built in reverse order, so reverse it to get the correct sequence.\n  \n  # 15. Append the 'USE' action to the path and return the complete sequence.\n  return path_to_target + [USE]", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:44:40.864512", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:44:41.998786", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  world_cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  game_grid = current_state.grid\n  \n  # Retrieve the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  primitive_id = world_cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not valid or not found in the game's index,\n    # it's impossible to collect, so return an empty action list.\n    return []\n\n  # Map human-readable action names to their numerical IDs for execution.\n  action_ids = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_ids['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_ids['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_ids['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_ids['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_ids['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas and their corresponding actions for BFS exploration.\n  # Each tuple is (change_in_x, change_in_y, action_id_to_perform).\n  possible_moves = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases Y)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X)\n  ]\n\n  # Get grid dimensions to enforce boundary checks during pathfinding.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = game_grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current starting position for the BFS.\n  start_agent_pos = current_state.pos\n\n  # BFS data structures:\n  # bfs_queue: stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  #            This allows reconstructing the path once the target is found.\n  # visited_cells: a set to keep track of positions already explored to prevent cycles\n  #                and ensure the shortest path is found (critical for unweighted graphs).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(start_agent_pos, [])]) \n  visited_cells = {start_agent_pos} \n\n  # Classify the primitive type to apply the correct collection logic at the goal.\n  is_grabbable = primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_id in env.world.workshop_indices\n  # Fixed features are environment entities like water, stone, or boundaries that\n  # are \"collected\" by simply being on their cell.\n  is_fixed_feature = (primitive_id == env.world.water_index or \n                      primitive_id == env.world.stone_index or \n                      primitive_id == world_cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  \n  # Perform Breadth-First Search to find the primitive.\n  while bfs_queue:\n    current_bfs_pos, actions_path = bfs_queue.popleft()\n\n    # Create a temporary CraftState object for the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's utility methods (like `next_to`) or\n    # inspect the grid content at this hypothetical position without modifying\n    # the actual environment state. The agent's direction and inventory are\n    # kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    hypothetical_state = craft.CraftState(\n        current_state.scenario, \n        current_state.grid, \n        current_bfs_pos, \n        current_state.dir, \n        current_state.inventory\n    )\n\n    # Check if the current `hypothetical_state` satisfies the collection goal.\n    # Since BFS explores layer by layer, the first path found is guaranteed to be the shortest.\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., 'WOOD', 'IRON', 'GRASS'), the agent needs to be\n      # adjacent to the item and then perform a 'USE' action to pick it up.\n      if hypothetical_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n        return actions_path + [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_fixed_feature:\n      # For workshops (e.g., 'WORKSHOP0') or fixed environment features (e.g., 'WATER', 'STONE'),\n      # 'collection' typically means simply reaching the cell where the item/feature is located.\n      # We check the grid content directly at the current position.\n      if hypothetical_state.grid[current_bfs_pos[0], current_bfs_pos[1], primitive_id] > 0:\n        return actions_path # No 'USE' action is typically required for these.\n    \n    # If the current position is not the goal, explore valid neighboring cells.\n    for dx, dy, action_id in possible_moves:\n      new_x, new_y = current_bfs_pos[0] + dx, current_bfs_pos[1] + dy\n      new_position = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if 0 <= new_x < grid_width and 0 <= new_y < grid_height:\n        # If this new position has not been visited yet during BFS.\n        if new_position not in visited_cells:\n          visited_cells.add(new_position)\n          # Add the new position and the updated action path to the queue.\n          bfs_queue.append((new_position, actions_path + [action_id]))\n  \n  # If the BFS completes and no path to the primitive was found (queue exhausted),\n  # return an empty list, indicating the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:45:40.522243", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by considering agent direction for 'USE' action.\"\"\"\n\n  # Helper to map action to resulting direction (assuming DMLab-style directions: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W)\n  def _get_dir_from_action(action, action_map):\n      if action == action_map['UP']:\n          return 0 # North\n      elif action == action_map['RIGHT']:\n          return 1 # East\n      elif action == action_map['DOWN']:\n          return 2 # South\n      elif action == action_map['LEFT']:\n          return 3 # West\n      return -1 # Should not happen for movement actions\n\n  # Helper to get the cell coordinates directly in front of the agent based on its direction\n  def _get_cell_in_front(pos, agent_dir):\n      x, y = pos\n      if agent_dir == 0: # North (UP)\n          return (x, y - 1)\n      elif agent_dir == 1: # East (RIGHT)\n          return (x + 1, y)\n      elif agent_dir == 2: # South (DOWN)\n          return (x, y + 1)\n      elif agent_dir == 3: # West (LEFT)\n          return (x - 1, y)\n      return (-1, -1) # Should not happen for valid directions\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy), their corresponding action ID, and the resulting agent direction\n  # Directions are typically 0=North, 1=East, 2=South, 3=West (matching DMLab conventions)\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP, 0),    # Move Up (North), agent faces North\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN, 2),   # Move Down (South), agent faces South\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT, 3),  # Move Left (West), agent faces West\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT, 1),  # Move Right (East), agent faces East\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position and initial direction\n  start_pos = state.pos\n  start_dir = state.dir \n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle unless it's the target.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, current_direction, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])]) \n  # Visited set tracks (position, direction) pairs to avoid redundant exploration and cycles\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)} \n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx))\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_dir, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # --- Goal Check ---\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      # Crucially, the 'USE' action interacts with the cell *in front* of the agent.\n      target_cell_coords = _get_cell_in_front(current_pos, current_dir)\n      \n      # Ensure the cell in front is within grid boundaries before checking its contents\n      if (0 <= target_cell_coords[0] < WIDTH and \n          0 <= target_cell_coords[1] < HEIGHT):\n          \n          # Check if the target primitive is present in the cell directly in front\n          if grid[target_cell_coords[0], target_cell_coords[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n              is_goal_reached = True\n              actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n    # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # --- Explore Neighbors ---\n    # For each possible movement action\n    for dx, dy, action_move, new_dir_after_move in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n      new_state_tuple = (new_pos, new_dir_after_move) # New state includes position and direction\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless we are specifically collecting 'BOUNDARY'.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY', it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        # Only add to queue if this (position, direction) state has not been visited and is not an obstacle\n        if new_state_tuple not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_state_tuple)\n          q.append((new_pos, new_dir_after_move, current_actions + [action_move]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:45:41.886180", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  # The Index class's __getitem__ method returns int or None.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx))\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      # Note: The grid stores counts, so > 0 means presence.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n    # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless we are specifically collecting 'BOUNDARY'.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY', it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:46:39.662303", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid # Current grid state (static for pathfinding)\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive from the cookbook index\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings for easier use\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for distinct collection logic:\n  is_grabbable_item = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  is_stationary_feature = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                           primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                           primitive_idx == cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  \n  # Optimization: If the primitive is grabbable and the agent already possesses it,\n  # no further actions are needed. The item is considered \"collected\".\n  if is_grabbable_item and state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Helper function to check if the primitive can be collected from a given (position, direction) state.\n  # This makes the main BFS loop cleaner by abstracting the goal logic.\n  def _check_collectable(pos: tuple[int, int], direction: int, target_idx: int) -> tuple[bool, list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the target primitive can be collected from the given agent position and direction.\n    \n    Args:\n        pos: Agent's current (x, y) position.\n        direction: Agent's current facing direction (0:DOWN, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:RIGHT).\n        target_idx: The integer ID of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple: (bool is_collectable, list_of_actions_to_complete_collection).\n        `is_collectable` is True if the primitive can be collected.\n        `list_of_actions_to_complete_collection` contains actions like [ACTION_USE] if needed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if is_grabbable_item:\n      # For grabbable items, the agent must be directly facing the item and then USE it.\n      fwd_x, fwd_y = pos\n      if direction == ACTION_UP:  # Direction 1\n          fwd_y -= 1\n      elif direction == ACTION_DOWN:  # Direction 0\n          fwd_y += 1\n      elif direction == ACTION_LEFT:  # Direction 2\n          fwd_x -= 1\n      elif direction == ACTION_RIGHT:  # Direction 3\n          fwd_x += 1\n      \n      # Check if the cell directly in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive.\n      if 0 <= fwd_x < WIDTH and 0 <= fwd_y < HEIGHT:\n        if grid[fwd_x, fwd_y, target_idx] > 0:\n          return True, [ACTION_USE] # Requires a 'USE' action\n      return False, []\n\n    elif is_workshop_location or is_stationary_feature:\n      # For workshops or stationary features, \"collection\" means simply being at their location.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the agent's current cell.\n      if grid[pos[0], pos[1], target_idx] > 0:\n        return True, [] # No additional action required, just presence\n      return False, []\n    \n    return False, [] # Fallback for unhandled primitive types (should ideally not be reached)\n\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS):\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, current_direction_int, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(state.pos, state.dir, [])]) \n  \n  # The visited set tracks (position, direction) pairs to prevent redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(state.pos, state.dir)} \n\n  # Variables to store the shortest complete path found during the BFS.\n  min_path_len = float('inf')\n  shortest_path_actions = []\n\n  # BFS loop: Continues until all reachable states are explored or a sufficiently short path is found.\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_dir, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Pruning optimization: If the current path to this state is already longer than\n    # or equal to the shortest complete path found so far, prune this branch as it cannot\n    # yield a shorter overall solution.\n    if len(current_actions) >= min_path_len:\n        continue\n\n    # Check if the primitive can be collected from the current agent's (position, direction) state using the helper.\n    is_collectable, final_collection_actions = _check_collectable(current_pos, current_dir, primitive_idx)\n    \n    # If the primitive can be collected from the current state:\n    if is_collectable:\n      # Construct the full sequence of actions for this particular path (movement + final collection actions).\n      path_to_collect = current_actions + final_collection_actions\n      \n      # If this complete path is shorter than the shortest one found so far, update the best path.\n      if len(path_to_collect) < min_path_len:\n        min_path_len = len(path_to_collect)\n        shortest_path_actions = path_to_collect\n      \n      # IMPORTANT: Do NOT break the BFS here. Continuing the search guarantees finding\n      # the globally shortest path. A slightly longer movement path to a (pos, dir) state\n      # might, when combined with the final collection action, still result in a shorter\n      # *total* sequence compared to other paths.\n\n    # Explore possible next states by simulating movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n    for action_to_take in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]:\n      # Create a temporary CraftState to simulate the effect of the action without altering\n      # the main environment state. The grid and inventory remain constant for pathfinding within this call.\n      temp_state_for_simulation = craft.CraftState(\n          state.scenario, state.grid, \n          current_pos, current_dir, state.inventory\n      )\n      \n      # Apply the movement action to the temporary state.\n      # The reward returned by step is not relevant for pathfinding here.\n      _, next_simulated_state = temp_state_for_simulation.step(action_to_take)\n      \n      next_pos = next_simulated_state.pos\n      next_dir = next_simulated_state.dir\n\n      # Define the new state tuple (position, direction) for tracking visited states.\n      next_state_tuple = (next_pos, next_dir)\n\n      # If this new (position, direction) state has not been visited yet,\n      # add it to the queue for future exploration and mark it as visited.\n      if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n        q.append((next_pos, next_dir, current_actions + [action_to_take]))\n  \n  # After BFS completes, return the shortest sequence of actions found to collect the primitive.\n  # If no path was found (e.g., primitive is unreachable), shortest_path_actions will remain empty.\n  return shortest_path_actions", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:46:40.929499", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:47:17.856544", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # (px, py)\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the primitive\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive not found in the cookbook, return empty actions\n    return []\n\n  # Improvement: Check if the primitive is in the set of grabbable items.\n  # If it's not a grabbable item (e.g., a workshop, boundary, water), it cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  # The 'collect' action in the DSL implies adding to inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Improvement: Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If it is, no further actions are needed to \"collect\" it.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Action integer mappings\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Directions mapping to actions for BFS path reconstruction\n  # (dx, dy) -> action (movement from current_pos to next_pos)\n  dir_to_action = {\n      (0, -1): UP,\n      (0, 1): DOWN,\n      (-1, 0): LEFT,\n      (1, 0): RIGHT,\n  }\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Identify impassable terrain indices.\n  # It's assumed that 'BOUNDARY' and 'WATER' cells are not traversable by the agent.\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_indices.add(cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  if 'WATER' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_indices.add(cookbook.index['WATER'])\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell is traversable\n  def is_cell_traversable(x, y):\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False  # Out of bounds\n      for imp_idx in impassable_indices:\n          if grid[x, y, imp_idx] == 1:\n              return False  # Contains an impassable object\n      return True\n\n  # Check if the agent's starting position is traversable. If not, no path is possible.\n  if not is_cell_traversable(agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1]):\n      return []\n\n  # Find all occurrences of the primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n\n  if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n    # Primitive not present on the current grid, return empty actions\n    return []\n\n  # Define the set of target cells for BFS.\n  # These are any cells from which the agent can successfully 'USE' the primitive.\n  # According to CraftState.next_to, this means any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # (including the cell itself) around a primitive's location.\n  bfs_target_cells = set()\n  for tx, ty in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around the primitive location\n    for dx_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = tx + dx_n, ty + dy_n\n        \n        # A potential target cell must be within grid bounds AND traversable by the agent\n        if is_cell_traversable(nx, ny):\n          bfs_target_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # If no valid traversable target cells exist, no path is possible\n  if not bfs_target_cells:\n      return []\n\n  # Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # Queue stores (current_x, current_y)\n  q = collections.deque([agent_pos])\n  # Visited set for faster lookups\n  visited = {agent_pos}\n  # Parent dictionary to reconstruct the path: {child_pos: parent_pos}\n  parent = {agent_pos: None} \n\n  target_found_pos = None\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos = q.popleft()\n    \n    # Check if the current position is one of our valid target cells\n    if current_pos in bfs_target_cells:\n      target_found_pos = current_pos\n      break # Found shortest path to a target cell, stop BFS\n\n    # Explore valid neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n    for dx, dy in [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]:\n      next_x, next_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries and is traversable\n      if not is_cell_traversable(next_x, next_y):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if the next position has already been visited\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        parent[next_pos] = current_pos # Store parent for path reconstruction\n        q.append(next_pos)\n  \n  # Path reconstruction\n  if target_found_pos is None:\n    # If the queue became empty and no target was found\n    return []\n  \n  path_to_target = []\n  current = target_found_pos\n  while parent[current] is not None:\n    prev = parent[current]\n    dx, dy = current[0] - prev[0], current[1] - prev[1]\n    path_to_target.append(dir_to_action[(dx, dy)])\n    current = prev\n  \n  path_to_target.reverse() # Path is built in reverse, so reverse it\n  \n  # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence.\n  return path_to_target + [USE]", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:47:19.114393", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the primitive\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive not found in the cookbook or an invalid primitive name was passed.\n    # Return empty actions as it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Early Exit 1: If the primitive is not a grabbable item (e.g., a workshop, boundary, water).\n  # The 'collect' action in the DSL implies adding to inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Early Exit 2: If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # No further actions are needed to \"collect\" it.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # (px, py)\n  \n  # Action integer mappings\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Directions mapping to actions for BFS path reconstruction\n  # (dx, dy) -> action (movement from current_pos to next_pos)\n  dir_to_action = {\n      (0, -1): UP,   # Up (decreasing Y)\n      (0, 1): DOWN,  # Down (increasing Y)\n      (-1, 0): LEFT, # Left (decreasing X)\n      (1, 0): RIGHT, # Right (increasing X)\n  }\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Identify impassable terrain indices.\n  # In CraftWorld, 'BOUNDARY' and 'WATER' are typically the only entities\n  # that completely block agent movement.\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  for item_name in ['BOUNDARY', 'WATER']:\n      if item_name in cookbook.index.contents:\n          impassable_indices.add(cookbook.index[item_name])\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell is traversable\n  def is_cell_traversable(x, y):\n      # Check if the coordinates are within grid bounds\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False  # Out of bounds\n\n      # Check if any identified impassable item occupies this cell\n      for imp_idx in impassable_indices:\n          if grid[x, y, imp_idx] == 1: # Assuming one-hot encoding for grid cells\n              return False  # Contains an impassable object\n      return True\n\n  # Preliminary check: If the agent's starting position is not traversable, no path can be formed.\n  if not is_cell_traversable(agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1]):\n      return []\n\n  # Find all grid locations where the primitive item exists\n  primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n\n  if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n    # Primitive not present on the current grid\n    return []\n\n  # Define the set of target cells for BFS.\n  # These are any traversable cells from which the agent can successfully 'USE' the primitive.\n  # The `CraftState.next_to` method indicates `USE` operates on the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent.\n  bfs_target_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive location (including the location itself)\n    for dx_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx_n, py + dy_n\n        \n        # Add to target cells if within grid bounds AND traversable by the agent\n        if is_cell_traversable(nx, ny):\n          bfs_target_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # If no valid traversable target cells exist (e.g., primitive is completely surrounded by impassable terrain)\n  if not bfs_target_cells:\n      return []\n\n  # Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # Queue stores (current_x, current_y) tuples.\n  q = collections.deque([agent_pos])\n  # Visited set to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {agent_pos} \n  # Parent dictionary to reconstruct the path: {child_pos: parent_pos}.\n  parent = {agent_pos: None} \n\n  target_found_pos = None\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos = q.popleft()\n    \n    # Check if the current position is one of our valid target cells\n    if current_pos in bfs_target_cells:\n      target_found_pos = current_pos\n      break # Found the shortest path to a suitable interaction cell, stop BFS.\n\n    # Explore valid neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n    for dx, dy in [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]: # Standard 4-directional moves (dx, dy)\n      next_x, next_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries, is traversable, and hasn't been visited yet\n      if is_cell_traversable(next_x, next_y) and next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        parent[next_pos] = current_pos # Store parent for path reconstruction\n        q.append(next_pos)\n  \n  # Path reconstruction\n  if target_found_pos is None:\n    # If the queue became empty and no path was found to any target cell\n    return []\n  \n  path_to_target = []\n  current = target_found_pos\n  while parent[current] is not None:\n    prev = parent[current]\n    # Calculate the movement direction from prev to current\n    dx, dy = current[0] - prev[0], current[1] - prev[1]\n    path_to_target.append(dir_to_action[(dx, dy)])\n    current = prev\n  \n  path_to_target.reverse() # Path is built in reverse, so reverse it to get correct order\n  \n  # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence.\n  return path_to_target + [USE]", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:48:02.972294", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive string is not known to the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state details\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Improvement from collect_v1:\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If it is, no actions are needed to \"collect\" it, as it's already collected.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # From collect_v1:\n  # Check if the primitive is actually a grabbable item.\n  # The 'collect' function implies acquiring an item into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is marked as non-grabbable in the world configuration,\n  # it cannot be 'collected' in this manner, so no actions are returned.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Grid and position details\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for each action\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # --- NEW IMPROVEMENT FOR collect_v2 ---\n  # Get the index for the 'BOUNDARY' entity to avoid moving into blocked cells.\n  # Assuming 'BOUNDARY' entities are static obstacles that prevent agent movement.\n  try:\n    boundary_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(\"BOUNDARY\")\n  except KeyError:\n    # If \"BOUNDARY\" is not defined, assume no explicit boundaries block movement beyond grid edges.\n    boundary_idx = -1 # A sentinel value indicating no boundary check needed\n  # --- END NEW IMPROVEMENT ---\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given position is next to (or on) the target primitive\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Check the 3x3 neighborhood around the current position\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor position is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # If the target primitive is found in this neighbor cell, return True\n          # We check if the count of the primitive at (nx, ny, target_idx) is greater than 0\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n\n  # Initialize BFS queue with the starting position and an empty path\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) # (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_position)\n  # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is next to (or on) the primitive, we've found a path\n    # We must be at a position from which we can USE the primitive.\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence of actions\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all possible moves from the current position\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n      \n      # --- NEW IMPROVEMENT FOR collect_v2 ---\n      # Check if the next position contains a 'BOUNDARY' entity (if boundary_idx is valid).\n      # If it does, it's blocked and cannot be traversed.\n      if boundary_idx != -1 and grid[next_x, next_y, boundary_idx] > 0:\n        continue\n      # --- END NEW IMPROVEMENT ---\n\n      # If the next position has not been visited, add it to the queue\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path is found (primitive is unreachable), return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:48:04.089763", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive string is not known to the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state details\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If it is, no actions are needed to \"collect\" it, as it's already collected.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is actually a grabbable item.\n  # The 'collect' function implies acquiring an item into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is marked as non-grabbable in the world configuration,\n  # it cannot be 'collected' in this manner, so no actions are returned.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Grid and position details\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for each action\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given position is next to (or on) the target primitive\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Check the 3x3 neighborhood around the current position\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighbor position is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # If the target primitive is found in this neighbor cell, return True\n          # We check if the count of the primitive at (nx, ny, target_idx) is greater than 0\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n\n  # NEW IMPROVEMENT FOR V2: Check if a cell is traversable (i.e., not an obstacle)\n  def is_traversable(check_pos, current_grid, world_non_grabbable_indices):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # A cell is traversable if it does not contain any item from the non_grabbable_indices set.\n    # This assumes that non-grabbable items like BOUNDARY, WATER, STONE, WORKSHOP are obstacles.\n    for non_grabbable_idx in world_non_grabbable_indices:\n      if current_grid[px, py, non_grabbable_idx] > 0:\n        return False # This cell contains an obstacle\n    return True # Cell is traversable\n\n  # Initialize BFS queue with the starting position and an empty path\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) # (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_position)\n  # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is next to (or on) the primitive, we've found a path\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence of actions\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all possible moves from the current position\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n      \n      # NEW IMPROVEMENT FOR V2: Check if the next position is traversable (obstacle avoidance)\n      if not is_traversable(next_pos, grid, env.world.non_grabbable_indices):\n        continue\n\n      # If the next position has not been visited, add it to the queue\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path is found (primitive is unreachable), return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:48:28.232224", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  # The Index class's __getitem__ method returns int or None.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle.\n  # Use cookbook.index.contents to safely check for 'BOUNDARY' existence.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  # Ensure robust check for boundary existence.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx))\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      # Note: The grid stores counts, so > 0 means presence.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n    # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless we are specifically collecting 'BOUNDARY'.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY', it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:48:29.525655", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  # The Index class's __getitem__ method returns int or None.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx))\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    # This is safe because we are finding a path, not simulating state changes.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      # Note: The grid stores counts, so > 0 means presence.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n    # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless we are specifically collecting 'BOUNDARY'.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY', it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:49:41.465516", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` with enhanced clarity and explicit reasoning.\n\n  Returns a list of actions to find, approach, and \"collect\" (interact via USE)\n  the specified primitive in the passed CraftLab environment. This involves\n  finding the shortest path on the grid using Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  to a location from which the 'USE' action can be effectively applied\n  to the primitive.\n\n  \"Collecting\" a primitive here means navigating to its vicinity (within\n  a 3x3 neighborhood, including the agent's current cell) and performing\n  the 'USE' action. For static environment elements like workshops or water,\n  'collecting' implies interacting with them, not necessarily picking them up.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation.\n      primitive (str): The string name of the primitive (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\", \"WORKSHOP0\")\n                       to be collected.\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of integer action IDs (e.g., UP, DOWN, USE)\n                 representing the shortest path to collect the primitive.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is not found or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # --- Helper Functions for BFS Logic ---\n\n  def _is_next_to_kind(check_x: int, check_y: int, kind_idx: int, current_grid: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if the specified 'kind_idx' is present in the 3x3 grid neighborhood\n      around the given (check_x, check_y) coordinates (inclusive of the center cell).\n      This simulates the CraftState.next_to() behavior.\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = check_x + dx, check_y + dy\n              # Ensure neighbor coordinates are within the grid boundaries\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n                  # Check if any quantity of the target kind is at this neighbor cell\n                  if current_grid[nx, ny, kind_idx] > 0:\n                      return True\n      return False\n\n  def _is_obstacle_kind(kind_idx_at_cell: int, target_primitive_idx: int, world_config: craft.CraftWorld) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"\n      Determines if a specific 'kind' present at a grid cell should be considered\n      an impassable obstacle for the agent's movement.\n\n      Assumptions for traversability:\n      1. The target primitive itself is generally traversable; the agent can move onto it.\n      2. 'Grabbable' items (e.g., WOOD, IRON) are always traversable; the agent can walk over them.\n      3. Specific 'non-grabbable' entities (like WORKSHOPS or WATER) are considered\n         traversable points of interaction, not movement blockers.\n      4. Other 'non-grabbable' entities (e.g., BOUNDARY walls, certain types of STONE\n         if designated as non-grabbable and non-interactive) are considered impassable.\n      \"\"\"\n      # If the cell contains the target primitive itself, it's always traversable\n      # (agent can move onto it to interact/collect).\n      if kind_idx_at_cell == target_primitive_idx:\n          return False\n      \n      # Check if the item is explicitly marked as non-grabbable.\n      if kind_idx_at_cell in world_config.non_grabbable_indices:\n          # Special non-grabbable entities that are traversable/interactive points:\n          if kind_idx_at_cell in world_config.workshop_indices or \\\n             kind_idx_at_cell == world_config.water_index:\n              return False  # These are traversable.\n          else:\n              # Any other non-grabbable item (e.g., boundary walls) is an obstacle.\n              return True\n      \n      # All grabbable items (not explicitly handled above) are assumed traversable.\n      return False\n\n  # --- Main Logic for Pathfinding ---\n\n  # 1. Map the string primitive name to its integer ID used by the environment.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized, it's impossible to collect.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract essential current state information from the environment.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's starting (x, y) coordinates\n  current_grid = current_state.grid # The current state of the game grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n  world_config = env.world # Access to global world configuration (e.g., non-grabbable items)\n\n  # 3. Obtain the integer mappings for movement and 'USE' actions from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible cardinal movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # This makes iterating through neighbors in BFS more structured.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move South (increase Y)\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move North (decrease Y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move West (decrease X)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move East (increase X)\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # The queue will store tuples of: (current_position (x, y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])])\n  # 'visited_positions' keeps track of all (x, y) coordinates that have been added to the queue,\n  # preventing redundant paths and infinite loops.\n  visited_positions = {initial_pos}\n\n  # 5. Execute BFS to find the shortest path to a collectable primitive.\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path_to_current_pos = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the agent, at `current_pos`, is in a position to 'USE' the primitive.\n      # This means the primitive must be in the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent.\n      if _is_next_to_kind(cx, cy, primitive_idx, current_grid):\n          # If a suitable position is found, append the 'USE' action to the path\n          # and return this complete sequence of actions.\n          path_to_current_pos.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path_to_current_pos\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighbors from the `current_pos`.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # First, validate that the 'next_pos' is within the defined grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n          # Next, determine if the cell at 'next_pos' contains any impassable obstacles.\n          is_impassable_cell = False\n          # Iterate through all possible 'kinds' that might be present at the 'next_pos' cell.\n          for k_idx_at_cell in range(current_grid.shape[2]):\n              # If a specific 'kind' is present (even in a small quantity)...\n              if current_grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx_at_cell] > 0:\n                  # ...check if that 'kind' constitutes an obstacle.\n                  if _is_obstacle_kind(k_idx_at_cell, primitive_idx, world_config):\n                      is_impassable_cell = True\n                      break # Found an obstacle, this cell is blocked; no need to check other kinds.\n          \n          if is_impassable_cell:\n              continue # Skip this 'next_pos' if it's blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # If the 'next_pos' is traversable and has not been visited in a shorter path,\n          # add it to the BFS queue for further exploration.\n          if next_pos not in visited_positions:\n              visited_positions.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared references in the queue.\n              # This ensures each path in the BFS is independent.\n              new_path = list(path_to_current_pos)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # If the BFS completes (queue becomes empty) and no path to an adjacent primitive\n  # was found, it implies the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:49:42.740040", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n    Returns a list of actions to find, move to, and collect the specified primitive from the environment grid.\n    This function uses Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation environment.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to be collected (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of integer action IDs (from `env.action_specs()`) that, when executed,\n                   will lead the agent to collect the desired primitive. Returns an empty list if\n                   the primitive is not found or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # Helper function to check if the target primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of a given cell.\n  # This is used to determine if the 'USE' action can be applied from that cell.\n  def _is_target_primitive_adjacent(\n      center_x: int, center_y: int, target_kind_idx: int, current_grid: np.ndarray\n  ) -> bool:\n      grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              neighbor_x, neighbor_y = center_x + dx, center_y + dy\n              # Ensure the neighbor coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n              if 0 <= neighbor_x < grid_width and 0 <= neighbor_y < grid_height:\n                  # Check if the target primitive kind exists at the neighbor cell.\n                  if current_grid[neighbor_x, neighbor_y, target_kind_idx] > 0:\n                      return True\n      return False\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a specific kind present at a grid cell\n  # makes that cell impassable for agent movement.\n  def _is_cell_impassable_by_kind(\n      kind_idx_at_cell: int, target_primitive_idx: int, world_config: craft.CraftWorld\n  ) -> bool:\n      # The target primitive itself is generally traversable; agent can move onto or through it.\n      if kind_idx_at_cell == target_primitive_idx:\n          return False\n      \n      # Check if the item at the cell is one of the non-grabbable entities.\n      if kind_idx_at_cell in world_config.non_grabbable_indices:\n          # Special non-grabbable entities like workshops or water are considered traversable\n          # interaction points, not movement blockers.\n          if kind_idx_at_cell in world_config.workshop_indices or \\\n             kind_idx_at_cell == world_config.water_index:\n              return False  # These are traversable.\n          else:\n              # Other non-grabbable items (e.g., \"BOUNDARY\" walls, some \"STONE\" configurations)\n              # are treated as impassable obstacles.\n              return True\n      \n      # Any other kind (typically grabbable items like \"WOOD\", \"IRON\", \"GRASS\")\n      # is considered traversable; the agent can move over them.\n      return False\n\n  # --- Main Logic of collect_v2 ---\n\n  # 1. Retrieve the numerical index for the target primitive from the environment's cookbook.\n  # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive) # Using .get() returns None if not found\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract essential information from the current environment state.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_agent_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's starting (x, y) coordinates.\n  current_grid = current_state.grid      # The current layout of the world grid.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape # Dimensions of the grid.\n  world_config = env.world               # Reference to the CraftWorld instance for environment rules.\n\n  # 3. Get the integer action mappings for movement and 'USE' from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement directions and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # This structure simplifies iterating through neighbors in the BFS.\n  movement_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # (dx, dy) for moving South (down on grid), action ID.\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # (dx, dy) for moving North (up on grid), action ID.\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving West (left on grid), action ID.\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # (dx, dy) for moving East (right on grid), action ID.\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(initial_agent_pos, [])])\n  # 'visited_positions' set keeps track of (x,y) positions already explored\n  # to prevent cycles and re-exploring paths unnecessarily.\n  visited_positions = {initial_agent_pos}\n\n  # 5. BFS Loop: Continue until the queue is empty or a path is found.\n  while bfs_queue:\n      current_pos, path_to_current_pos = bfs_queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the agent, at the current position (cx, cy), can perform the 'USE' action\n      # to collect the target primitive. This means the primitive must be in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n      if _is_target_primitive_adjacent(cx, cy, primitive_idx, current_grid):\n          # If a suitable position is found, append the 'USE' action and return the complete path.\n          path_to_current_pos.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path_to_current_pos\n\n      # If not yet at a collection point, explore all four cardinal neighboring cells.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id_for_move in movement_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # a. Boundary Check: Ensure the next position is within the grid limits.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # b. Obstacle Check: Determine if the cell at 'next_pos' is traversable.\n          # A cell is considered impassable if any of the 'kinds' present in it are obstacles.\n          is_next_cell_impassable = False\n          # Iterate through all possible 'kinds' that might be at (next_x, next_y).\n          for kind_id_at_next_cell in range(current_grid.shape[2]):\n              # If a specific kind is present at the next cell...\n              if current_grid[next_x, next_y, kind_id_at_next_cell] > 0:\n                  # ...check if that kind makes the cell an obstacle.\n                  if _is_cell_impassable_by_kind(kind_id_at_next_cell, primitive_idx, world_config):\n                      is_next_cell_impassable = True\n                      break  # Found an obstacle, no need to check other kinds in this cell.\n          \n          if is_next_cell_impassable:\n              continue  # Skip this next position if it's blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # c. Visited Check: If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited_positions:\n              visited_positions.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared references in the queue.\n              new_path = list(path_to_current_pos)\n              new_path.append(action_id_for_move)\n              bfs_queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # 6. If the BFS completes (queue is empty) and no path to collect the primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:50:26.909490", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by adding obstacle avoidance.\"\"\"\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Get the current state of the environment\n  state = env._current_state\n  actions = []\n\n  # 3. Check if the agent is already adjacent to the primitive\n  # If so, just perform the USE action to collect/interact with it\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n    return actions\n\n  # 4. Initialize grid dimensions and agent position\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the set of non-grabbable indices to identify obstacles (impassable cells)\n  impassable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # 5. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      # Check if this cell contains the primitive\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, return an empty list\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any cell that is adjacent to any instance of the primitive.\n  #    Queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_actions_so_far)\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  best_path_to_adjacent = None\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding action indices\n  # Note: `env.action_specs()` provides the mapping from action names to integers\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), env.action_specs()['DOWN']),\n      ((0, -1), env.action_specs()['UP']),\n      ((1, 0), env.action_specs()['RIGHT']),\n      ((-1, 0), env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos, path = q.popleft()\n    curr_x, curr_y = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive locations\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_locations:\n      # Manhattan distance of 1 means it's adjacent\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) + abs(curr_y - target_y) == 1:\n        best_path_to_adjacent = path\n        break  # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n    \n    if best_path_to_adjacent:\n      break  # Path found, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for (dx, dy), action_idx in moves:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # NEW: Check for obstacles in the next position\n      # A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      # The agent cannot move into cells with non-grabbable items.\n      # We check if any of the non_grabbable_indices exist at the next_pos.\n      if any(grid[next_x, next_y, k] > 0 for k in impassable_indices):\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If the cell is not an obstacle and not visited, add to queue\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        new_path = path + [action_idx]\n        q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # 7. If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the USE action\n  if best_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n    actions.extend(best_path_to_adjacent)\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:50:28.141932", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  actions = []\n\n  # 3. Check if the agent is already adjacent to the primitive\n  # If so, just perform the USE action to collect/interact with it\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n    return actions\n\n  # 4. Initialize grid dimensions and agent position\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 5. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      # Check if this cell contains the primitive\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, return an empty list\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any cell that is adjacent to any instance of the primitive.\n  #    Queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_actions_so_far)\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  best_path_to_adjacent = None\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding action indices\n  # Note: `env.action_specs()` provides the mapping from action names to integers\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), env.action_specs()['DOWN']),\n      ((0, -1), env.action_specs()['UP']),\n      ((1, 0), env.action_specs()['RIGHT']),\n      ((-1, 0), env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  ]\n\n  # Define explicitly impassable indices based on common game conventions.\n  # Water and Boundary are usually unwalkable. Other non-grabbable items like Workshops\n  # are typically locations one can walk onto.\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  # Add water_index as an impassable obstacle\n  impassable_indices.add(env.world.water_index)\n  # Add boundary index as an impassable obstacle if it exists in the cookbook\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in env.world.cookbook.index.contents:\n    impassable_indices.add(env.world.cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  \n  # Helper function to check if a given cell (x, y) is blocked by an impassable item\n  def is_blocked(x, y):\n    for idx in impassable_indices:\n      if grid[x, y, idx] > 0:\n        return True\n    return False\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos, path = q.popleft()\n    curr_x, curr_y = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive locations\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_locations:\n      # Manhattan distance of 1 means it's adjacent\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) + abs(curr_y - target_y) == 1:\n        best_path_to_adjacent = path\n        break  # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n    \n    if best_path_to_adjacent:\n      break  # Path found, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for (dx, dy), action_idx in moves:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if the next position has already been visited\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Check if the next position is blocked by an impassable obstacle (NEW improvement)\n      if is_blocked(next_x, next_y):\n        continue\n\n      # If the cell is valid, not visited, and not blocked, add it to the queue\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      new_path = path + [action_idx]\n      q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # 7. If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the USE action\n  if best_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n    actions.extend(best_path_to_adjacent)\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:51:26.501222", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # The requested primitive name is not recognized by the environment's cookbook.\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve current state information.\n  state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory. If so, no collection actions are needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # The 'collect' function implies obtaining the item in inventory.\n  # If the primitive is not in the set of items that can be picked up (grabbable),\n  # it cannot be \"collected\" in the sense of adding to inventory.\n  # Examples like BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP0 are in the DSL's 'primitive' list\n  # but are not designed to be picked up by the agent.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Get grid dimensions and agent's initial position.\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer action mappings from the environment for movement and 'USE'.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION),\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION),\n  ]\n\n  # Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any cell that is adjacent to the target primitive.\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])]) # Stores (current_position, path_taken_to_reach_here).\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant computations.\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to (or on the same cell as)\n      # any of the primitive's known locations. This allows for the 'USE' action.\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # A cell is considered \"adjacent\" if it's within 1 unit of Manhattan distance\n          # in both x and y, forming a 3x3 square (including the center).\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent cell is found, append the 'USE' action and return\n          # the complete sequence of actions (movement path + use action).\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the next cell is traversable or an impassable obstacle.\n          # This logic is based on v1's improved traversability check.\n          is_impassable = False\n          for k_idx in range(num_kinds): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If there's something of kind k_idx at this cell...\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx:\n                      # Agent can move onto the primitive's own cell.\n                      pass \n                  elif k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                      # Some non-grabbable entities are traversable (e.g., workshops, water)\n                      # while others are blocking (e.g., solid walls or boundaries).\n                      if k_idx in env.world.workshop_indices or k_idx == env.world.water_index:\n                          pass # Allow movement onto these specific non-grabbables\n                      else:\n                          # Other non-grabbable entities not explicitly allowed are obstacles.\n                          is_impassable = True\n                          break # This cell is blocked by an impassable object.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path if the cell is blocked.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive is found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position given the current grid.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:51:27.656384", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`. Finds the shortest path to a primitive and collects it.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute to collect the primitive.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Map the primitive name to its integer ID.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized by the environment's cookbook,\n      # it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If so, no collection actions are needed.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Verify if the primitive is a 'grabbable' item.\n  # The 'collect' action in this DSL implies adding the item to the agent's inventory.\n  # If the item is not in the set of entities that can be picked up, it cannot be collected.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      # Examples: 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER', 'WORKSHOP0' are primitives but not grabbable.\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Extract current state information and action mappings for pathfinding.\n  agent_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid.\n  grid = current_state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer action IDs for movement and 'USE' from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  # These are (dx, dy) tuples relative to the current position.\n  move_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move one step down (increase y)\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move one step up (decrease y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move one step left (decrease x)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move one step right (increase x)\n  ]\n\n  # 5. Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # If the cell contains at least one unit of the target primitive.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The goal is to find a path to any cell that is adjacent to (or on the same cell as)\n  # a primitive location, enabling the 'USE' action to collect it.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {agent_pos} # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant computations.\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive's known locations.\n      # A cell is considered \"adjacent\" if it's within 1 unit of Manhattan distance\n      # (i.e., it's in the 3x3 neighborhood, including the center cell).\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(cx - px) <= 1 and abs(cy - py) <= 1:\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break # Found an adjacent primitive location.\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # If an adjacent location is found, append the 'USE' action to the path\n          # and return the complete sequence of actions (movement path + use action).\n          path_so_far.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path_so_far\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the next cell is traversable or an impassable obstacle.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Check all kinds of entities that might be present in the next cell.\n          for k_idx in range(num_kinds): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If something of kind k_idx exists at this cell...\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx:\n                      # If the cell contains the target primitive itself, it is traversable.\n                      # The agent needs to be able to move onto or through the primitive's location.\n                      pass \n                  elif k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                      # If it's a non-grabbable entity:\n                      # Some non-grabbables (like workshops and water) are traversable,\n                      # others (like boundaries/solid walls) are impassable.\n                      if k_idx in env.world.workshop_indices or k_idx == env.world.water_index:\n                          pass # Allow movement onto workshops and water.\n                      else:\n                          # Other non-grabbable entities are considered obstacles.\n                          is_impassable = True\n                          break # This cell is blocked, no need to check further kinds.\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path if the cell is blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path_so_far) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive is found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position given the current grid layout.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:52:32.810077", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:52:33.903582", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` with enhanced clarity and modularity.\n\n  Returns a list of actions to find, approach, and \"collect\" (interact via USE)\n  the specified primitive in the passed CraftLab environment. This involves\n  finding the shortest path on the grid using Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  to a location from which the 'USE' action can be effectively applied\n  to the primitive.\n\n  \"Collecting\" a primitive here means navigating to its vicinity (within\n  a 3x3 neighborhood, including the agent's current cell) and performing\n  the 'USE' action. For static environment elements like workshops or water,\n  'collecting' implies interacting with them, not necessarily picking them up.\n\n  This version refactors the core logic into helper functions for better\n  readability and maintainability, building upon the BFS foundation.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation.\n      primitive (str): The string name of the primitive (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\", \"WORKSHOP0\")\n                       to be collected.\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of integer action IDs (e.g., UP, DOWN, USE)\n                 representing the shortest path to collect the primitive.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is not found or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # --- Helper Functions for BFS Logic ---\n\n  def _is_next_to_kind(check_x: int, check_y: int, kind_idx: int, current_grid: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if the specified 'kind_idx' is present in the 3x3 grid neighborhood\n      around the given (check_x, check_y) coordinates (inclusive of the center cell).\n      This simulates the CraftState.next_to() behavior for goal checking.\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = check_x + dx, check_y + dy\n              # Ensure neighbor coordinates are within the grid boundaries\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n                  # Check if any quantity of the target kind is at this neighbor cell\n                  if current_grid[nx, ny, kind_idx] > 0:\n                      return True\n      return False\n\n  def _is_obstacle_kind(kind_idx_at_cell: int, target_primitive_idx: int, world_config: craft.CraftWorld) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"\n      Determines if a specific 'kind' present at a grid cell should be considered\n      an impassable obstacle for the agent's movement.\n\n      Assumptions for traversability:\n      - The target primitive itself is always traversable (agent can move onto it to interact).\n      - 'Grabbable' items (e.g., WOOD, IRON) are always traversable (agent can walk over them).\n      - Specific 'non-grabbable' entities (like WORKSHOPS or WATER) are considered\n        traversable points of interaction, not movement blockers.\n      - Other 'non-grabbable' entities (e.g., 'BOUNDARY' walls, some specific types of STONE\n        if designated as non-grabbable and non-interactive) are considered impassable.\n      \"\"\"\n      # If the cell contains the target primitive itself, it's always traversable\n      # (agent can move onto it to interact/collect).\n      if kind_idx_at_cell == target_primitive_idx:\n          return False\n      \n      # Check if the item is explicitly marked as non-grabbable by the world config.\n      if kind_idx_at_cell in world_config.non_grabbable_indices:\n          # Special non-grabbable entities that are traversable/interactive points:\n          if kind_idx_at_cell in world_config.workshop_indices or\\\n             kind_idx_at_cell == world_config.water_index:\n              return False  # These are traversable interaction points.\n          else:\n              # Any other non-grabbable item (e.g., boundary walls) is an obstacle.\n              return True\n      \n      # All grabbable items (not explicitly handled as non-grabbable above) are assumed traversable.\n      return False\n\n  # --- Main Logic for Pathfinding ---\n\n  # 1. Map the string primitive name to its integer ID used by the environment.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized, it's impossible to collect.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract essential current state information from the environment.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's starting (x, y) coordinates\n  current_grid = current_state.grid # The current state of the game grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n  world_config = env.world # Access to global world configuration (e.g., non-grabbable items)\n\n  # 3. Obtain the integer mappings for movement and 'USE' actions from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible cardinal movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # This makes iterating through neighbors in BFS more structured.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move South (increase Y)\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move North (decrease Y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move West (decrease X)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move East (increase X)\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # The queue will store tuples of: (current_position (x, y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])])\n  # 'visited_positions' keeps track of all (x, y) coordinates that have been added to the queue,\n  # preventing redundant paths and infinite loops.\n  visited_positions = {initial_pos}\n\n  # 5. Execute BFS to find the shortest path to a collectable primitive.\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path_to_current_pos = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the agent, at `current_pos`, is in a position to 'USE' the primitive.\n      # This means the primitive must be in the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent.\n      if _is_next_to_kind(cx, cy, primitive_idx, current_grid):\n          # If a suitable position is found, append the 'USE' action to the path\n          # and return this complete sequence of actions.\n          path_to_current_pos.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path_to_current_pos\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighbors from the `current_pos`.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # First, validate that the 'next_pos' is within the defined grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n          # Next, determine if the cell at 'next_pos' contains any impassable obstacles.\n          is_impassable_cell = False\n          # Iterate through all possible 'kinds' that might be present at the 'next_pos' cell.\n          for k_idx_at_cell in range(current_grid.shape[2]):\n              # If a specific 'kind' is present (even in a small quantity)...\n              if current_grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx_at_cell] > 0:\n                  # ...check if that 'kind' constitutes an obstacle.\n                  if _is_obstacle_kind(k_idx_at_cell, primitive_idx, world_config):\n                      is_impassable_cell = True\n                      break # Found an obstacle, this cell is blocked; no need to check other kinds.\n          \n          if is_impassable_cell:\n              continue # Skip this 'next_pos' if it's blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # If the 'next_pos' is traversable and has not been visited in a shorter path,\n          # add it to the BFS queue for further exploration.\n          if next_pos not in visited_positions:\n              visited_positions.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared references in the queue.\n              # This ensures each path in the BFS is independent.\n              new_path = list(path_to_current_pos)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # If the BFS completes (queue becomes empty) and no path to an adjacent primitive\n  # was found, it implies the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:53:34.176169", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    # Attempt to get the integer index for the primitive string from the cookbook's index.\n    # This operation can raise a KeyError if the primitive name is not recognized by the environment.\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is unknown to the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    # Return an empty list of actions as no plan can be formed.\n    return []\n\n  # Get the current state of the environment, which includes the agent's inventory,\n  # position, and the grid layout.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Optimization: Check if the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent already possesses at least one unit of the primitive, there's no need\n  # to collect more, so return an empty list of actions.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Constraint Check: Determine if the primitive is a 'grabbable' item.\n  # The 'collect' function is intended for acquiring items into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is defined as 'non-grabbable' (e.g., static environment features\n  # like workshops, water, or boundaries that cannot be picked up), it cannot be collected\n  # using this method. In such cases, no collection actions are possible.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Extract relevant information from the current state: the grid dimensions and\n  # the agent's starting position.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n\n  # Retrieve the integer mappings for various actions from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE'] # The action typically used to interact with or pick up items.\n\n  # Define the change in coordinates for each movement action.\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # Initialize a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # A set to keep track of visited grid positions to avoid redundant explorations and cycles.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop: Continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft() # Get the next position and its path from the queue.\n\n    # Improvement for collect_v2:\n    # Instead of re-implementing the 'next_to' logic, we leverage the existing\n    # CraftState.next_to method. To do this, we create a temporary CraftState\n    # instance that has its position set to the `curr_pos` from our BFS.\n    # Other state attributes (grid, scenario, direction, inventory) can be copied\n    # from the actual current_state, as they don't change during pathfinding and\n    # are needed for the CraftState constructor, but don't affect the `next_to` check itself.\n    temp_state = craft.CraftState(\n        scenario=current_state.scenario,\n        grid=current_state.grid,\n        pos=curr_pos,\n        dir=current_state.dir, # Direction is not relevant for next_to, but required by constructor\n        inventory=current_state.inventory # Inventory is not relevant for next_to, but required by constructor\n    )\n    \n    # Use the CraftState's built-in method to check if the current BFS position\n    # is next to the target primitive. This abstracts away the 3x3 neighborhood check.\n    if temp_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n      # Append the `ACTION_USE` to the current path and return the complete sequence of actions.\n      # This path represents the shortest sequence of moves to get next to the primitive,\n      # followed by the action to collect it.\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # If the primitive is not yet collectible from `curr_pos`, explore all possible moves\n    # from the current position.\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Validate the next position: ensure it is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip moves that go out of bounds.\n\n      # If the `next_pos` has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      # This ensures the BFS finds the shortest path by processing layers level by level.\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos) # Mark the new position as visited.\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action])) # Add the new position and its extended path to the queue.\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue is empty, it means no path was found to reach\n  # and collect the primitive from the initial state.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:53:35.388022", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by considering impassable terrain during pathfinding.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  try:\n    # Attempt to get the integer index for the primitive string from the cookbook's index.\n    # This operation can raise a KeyError if the primitive name is not recognized by the environment.\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is unknown to the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    # Return an empty list of actions as no plan can be formed.\n    return []\n\n  # Get the current state of the environment, which includes the agent's inventory,\n  # position, and the grid layout.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Optimization: Check if the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent already possesses at least one unit of the primitive, there's no need\n  # to collect more, so return an empty list of actions.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Constraint Check: Determine if the primitive is a 'grabbable' item.\n  # If the primitive is defined as 'non-grabbable' (e.g., static environment features\n  # like workshops, water, or boundaries that cannot be picked up), it cannot be collected\n  # using this method. In such cases, no collection actions are possible.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Extract relevant information from the current state: the grid dimensions and\n  # the agent's starting position.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the integer mappings for various actions from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define the change in coordinates for each movement action.\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n\n  # Determine which entities are considered impassable terrain.\n  # We assume any non-grabbable environment entity that is NOT a workshop is impassable.\n  # Convert workshop_indices to a set for efficient lookup.\n  workshop_indices_set = set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  impassable_terrain_indices = set()\n  for env_kind_idx in env.world.cookbook.environment:\n    if env_kind_idx not in workshop_indices_set:\n      impassable_terrain_indices.add(env_kind_idx)\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a given `check_pos` (agent's potential position)\n  # is adjacent to (or directly on) the target `primitive_idx` within the `current_grid`.\n  # This condition typically allows the `ACTION_USE` to be effective for collection.\n  def is_next_to_target(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid):\n    px, py = check_pos\n    # Iterate through a 3x3 neighborhood (including the center cell) around `check_pos`.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the neighboring coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n          # Check if the target primitive has a non-zero count at this neighboring cell.\n          if current_grid[nx, ny, target_idx] > 0:\n            return True # Target primitive found, meaning agent is in a position to use it.\n    return False # Target primitive not found in the neighborhood.\n\n  # Initialize a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # A set to keep track of visited grid positions to avoid redundant explorations and cycles.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop: Continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, path = q.popleft() # Get the next position and its path from the queue.\n\n    # Check if the agent, at the `curr_pos`, is in a state to collect the primitive.\n    # If `is_next_to_target` is true, we have found a valid position to perform `ACTION_USE`.\n    if is_next_to_target(curr_pos, primitive_idx, grid):\n      # Append the `ACTION_USE` to the current path and return the complete sequence of actions.\n      # This path represents the shortest sequence of moves to get next to the primitive,\n      # followed by the action to collect it.\n      return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # If the primitive is not yet collectible from `curr_pos`, explore all possible moves\n    # from the current position.\n    for action, delta in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      dx, dy = delta\n      next_x, next_y = curr_pos[0] + dx, curr_pos[1] + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Validate the next position: ensure it is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip moves that go out of bounds.\n\n      # NEW IMPROVEMENT FOR COLLECT_V2: Check if the next position contains impassable terrain.\n      is_impassable_path = False\n      for kind_idx in impassable_terrain_indices:\n        # Check if the cell at `next_pos` contains any quantity of an impassable kind.\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, kind_idx] > 0:\n          is_impassable_path = True\n          break # Found impassable terrain, no need to check other kinds in this cell.\n      \n      if is_impassable_path:\n        continue # Skip this move if it leads to impassable terrain.\n\n      # If the `next_pos` has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      # This ensures the BFS finds the shortest path by processing layers level by level.\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos) # Mark the new position as visited.\n        q.append((next_pos, path + [action])) # Add the new position and its extended path to the queue.\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue is empty, it means no path was found to reach\n  # and collect the primitive from the initial state.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:54:55.868985", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  # The Index class's __getitem__ method returns int or None.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # --- IMPROVEMENT for v2: Check if primitive is already in inventory ---\n  # If the agent already possesses the primitive, no further actions are needed to \"collect\" it.\n  # This interprets \"use already available items\" as fulfilling the collection goal if already held.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx))\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      # Note: The grid stores counts, so > 0 means presence.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n    # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless we are specifically collecting 'BOUNDARY'.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY', it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:54:56.982364", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:55:44.240296", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  actions = []\n\n  # 3. Check if the agent is already adjacent to the primitive\n  # If so, just perform the USE action to collect/interact with it\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n    return actions\n\n  # 4. Initialize grid dimensions and agent position\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = grid.shape # N_KINDS is needed to check all layers of a cell\n\n  # Get indices for known non-walkable terrain from world configuration\n  # These are typically hard obstacles that agent cannot step onto.\n  water_idx = env.world.water_index\n  stone_idx = env.world.stone_index\n  # Workshop indices are typically non-grabbable but are traversable (agent can stand on them).\n  # We should ensure our obstacle logic handles this correctly.\n\n  # 5. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      # Check if this cell contains the primitive\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, return an empty list\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any cell that is adjacent to any instance of the primitive.\n  #    Queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_actions_so_far)\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  best_path_to_adjacent = None\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding action indices\n  # Note: `env.action_specs()` provides the mapping from action names to integers\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), env.action_specs()['DOWN']),\n      ((0, -1), env.action_specs()['UP']),\n      ((1, 0), env.action_specs()['RIGHT']),\n      ((-1, 0), env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos, path = q.popleft()\n    curr_x, curr_y = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive locations\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_locations:\n      # Manhattan distance of 1 means it's adjacent\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) + abs(curr_y - target_y) == 1:\n        best_path_to_adjacent = path\n        break  # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n    \n    if best_path_to_adjacent:\n      break  # Path found, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for (dx, dy), action_idx in moves:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Check if the next position is an obstacle.\n      # A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains water or stone,\n      # as these typically block movement in CraftWorld.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for k_idx in range(N_KINDS):\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If there's an item of kind k_idx at this cell\n          if k_idx == water_idx or k_idx == stone_idx:\n            is_obstacle = True\n            break # Found a blocking item, no need to check further for this cell\n      \n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Skip this next_pos as it's an impassable obstacle\n\n      # 3. Check if the next position has already been visited\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        new_path = path + [action_idx]\n        q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # 7. If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the USE action\n  if best_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n    actions.extend(best_path_to_adjacent)\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:55:45.435184", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` that avoids obstacles.\"\"\"\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  actions = []\n\n  # If the agent is already adjacent to the primitive, just perform the USE action\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n    return actions\n\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Identify impassable obstacles based on CraftWorld's definition.\n  # A cell is an obstacle if it contains a non-grabbable item that is not a workshop.\n  # This implies workshops are generally walkable, while water, stone, etc., are not.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # We're looking for cells *adjacent* to these locations.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, return an empty list\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # to any cell that is adjacent to any instance of the primitive.\n  # Queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_actions_so_far)\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  best_path_to_adjacent = None\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding action indices\n  moves = [\n      ((0, 1), env.action_specs()['DOWN']),\n      ((0, -1), env.action_specs()['UP']),\n      ((1, 0), env.action_specs()['RIGHT']),\n      ((-1, 0), env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    current_pos, path = q.popleft()\n    curr_x, curr_y = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any of the primitive locations\n    # If it is, this 'path' is a candidate. Since it's BFS, the first found is shortest.\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_locations:\n      # Manhattan distance of 1 means it's adjacent\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) + abs(curr_y - target_y) == 1:\n        best_path_to_adjacent = path\n        break  # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n    \n    if best_path_to_adjacent:\n      break  # Path found, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for (dx, dy), action_idx in moves:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if the next position contains an impassable obstacle\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for kind_id in impassable_kinds:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, kind_id] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      \n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move to this cell, it's an obstacle\n\n      # If the cell is walkable and not visited, add it to the queue\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        new_path = path + [action_idx]\n        q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n  \n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, extend actions with the path and the USE action\n  if best_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n    actions.extend(best_path_to_adjacent)\n    actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:56:44.919526", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx))\n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    # This is safe because we are finding a path, not simulating state changes.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      # Note: The grid stores counts, so > 0 means presence.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n    # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless we are specifically collecting 'BOUNDARY'.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY', it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:56:46.052398", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define mappings for movement actions to resulting agent directions\n  # CraftState directions are typically: 0:N (Up), 1:E (Right), 2:S (Down), 3:W (Left)\n  # Movement actions implicitly set the agent's facing direction.\n  action_to_dir = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 1,\n      ACTION_DOWN: 2,\n      ACTION_LEFT: 3,\n  }\n\n  # Define delta coordinates for each direction to find the cell in front of the agent\n  dir_to_delta = {\n      0: (0, -1), # North (Up)\n      1: (1, 0),  # East (Right)\n      2: (0, 1),  # South (Down)\n      3: (-1, 0), # West (Left)\n  }\n\n  # Grid dimensions\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's initial state (position, direction)\n  start_pos = state.pos\n  start_dir = state.dir # Current direction of the agent\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. 'BOUNDARY' is the most common explicit obstacle.\n  impassable_kind_idx = None\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n      impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY']\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, current_direction, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])]) \n  # Visited set stores (position, direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)} \n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone.\n  # If the target is 'BOUNDARY', it's treated as a stationary primitive that can be \"collected\" by reaching it.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index)\n  if impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx:\n      is_stationary_primitive = True\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_dir, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Goal Check:\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items, the agent must be directly facing the item to USE it.\n      dx, dy = dir_to_delta[current_dir]\n      front_x, front_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n\n      # Check if the cell in front is within bounds and contains the primitive\n      if 0 <= front_x < WIDTH and 0 <= front_y < HEIGHT:\n        if grid[front_x, front_y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n          is_goal_reached = True\n          actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n          \n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary: \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately (BFS guarantees the shortest path in unweighted graphs).\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors: Try all 4 movement actions\n    for action in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]:\n      new_dir = action_to_dir[action]\n      dx, dy = dir_to_delta[new_dir] # The movement delta is based on the direction the action causes the agent to face\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n      new_state_node = (new_pos, new_dir) # The state node includes both position and direction\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell unless 'BOUNDARY' is the target primitive.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_state_node not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_state_node)\n          q.append((new_pos, new_dir, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T00:57:36.189926", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by explicitly handling non-grabbable primitives and ensuring path traversability.\"\"\"\n  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # (px, py)\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the primitive\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized (e.g., not in the cookbook's index), return empty actions.\n    return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is a non-grabbable item.\n  # If it cannot be picked up into inventory, it cannot be \"collected\".\n  # In such cases, return an empty list of actions as this 'collect' operation is not applicable.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Action integer mappings from the environment's action specifications\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Mapping of (dx, dy) movement vectors to corresponding action indices.\n  # This is used to reconstruct the path after BFS.\n  dir_to_action = {\n      (0, -1): UP,   # Move Up (decreases Y coordinate)\n      (0, 1): DOWN,  # Move Down (increases Y coordinate)\n      (-1, 0): LEFT, # Move Left (decreases X coordinate)\n      (1, 0): RIGHT, # Move Right (increases X coordinate)\n  }\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Identify indices of entities that block agent movement.\n  # In CraftWorld, 'BOUNDARY' and 'WATER' are typically impassable.\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  for item_name in ['BOUNDARY', 'WATER']:\n      if item_name in cookbook.index.contents:\n          impassable_indices.add(cookbook.index[item_name])\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a given grid cell (x, y) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_cell_traversable(x, y):\n      # Check if coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False  # Out of bounds\n\n      # Check if the cell contains any impassable objects.\n      for imp_idx in impassable_indices:\n          if grid[x, y, imp_idx] == 1: # If the impassable item is present at this cell\n              return False  # Not traversable\n      return True # Cell is within bounds and does not contain impassable objects\n\n  # If the agent's current position is not traversable (e.g., spawned in water or a boundary),\n  # no path can be found, so return an empty list immediately.\n  if not is_cell_traversable(agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1]):\n      return []\n\n  # Find all locations on the grid where the target primitive is present.\n  primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, return empty actions.\n  if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine the set of target cells for the BFS.\n  # These are any traversable cells from which the agent can successfully 'USE' the primitive.\n  # The `CraftState.next_to` method checks the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent's position.\n  bfs_target_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive's location.\n    for dx_neighbor in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_neighbor in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx, ny = px + dx_neighbor, py + dy_neighbor\n        \n        # Add a cell to target_cells if it's within bounds and traversable.\n        if is_cell_traversable(nx, ny):\n          bfs_target_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # If no valid traversable cells from which to USE the primitive exist (e.g., primitive\n  # is entirely surrounded by impassable terrain), then no path can be found.\n  if not bfs_target_cells:\n      return []\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_coordinates, list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  # 'visited' set keeps track of cells already added to the queue to prevent cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {agent_pos}\n\n  while q:\n    current_coords, current_path = q.popleft()\n    \n    # If the current position is one of the valid target cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if current_coords in bfs_target_cells:\n      # Append the USE action, as the agent is now in a position to interact with the primitive.\n      return current_path + [USE]\n\n    # Explore valid adjacent cells (4-directional movement: Up, Down, Left, Right).\n    for dx, dy in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]: # Standard cardinal directions\n      next_x, next_y = current_coords[0] + dx, current_coords[1] + dy\n      next_coords = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is traversable and has not been visited yet.\n      if is_cell_traversable(next_x, next_y) and next_coords not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_coords)\n        # Create a new path by appending the action required to move to `next_coords`.\n        next_path = current_path + [dir_to_action[(dx, dy)]]\n        q.append((next_coords, next_path))\n  \n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path was found to any target cell,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
