{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T01:20:02.501389", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`, combining the most efficient and clear aspects of previous versions.\n\n    This version pre-calculates all valid 'interaction cells' (where a 'USE' action\n    can collect the primitive) and uses a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the\n    shortest path to any of these cells, followed by the 'USE' action. It also\n    includes checks for already having the item and ensures only grabbable items\n    are targeted for collection.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation environment.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to be collected (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of integer action IDs (movement and USE) to execute.\n                   Returns an empty list if the primitive is unreachable, not grabbable,\n                   or already in the agent's inventory.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  def _is_traversable(x: int, y: int, grid: np.ndarray, world_data: craft.CraftWorld) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"Helper function to determine if a grid cell is traversable by the agent.\"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n      # Check if the coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False  # Out of bounds.\n\n      # Iterate through all possible entity kinds in the environment.\n      for k_idx in range(num_kinds):\n          # If there's any entity of kind k_idx present at this cell (x, y).\n          if grid[x, y, k_idx] > 0:\n              # A cell is considered impassable if it contains a non-grabbable\n              # entity that is NOT a workshop and NOT water. These exceptions\n              # (workshops, water) are typically traversable or special interaction points.\n              if k_idx in world_data.non_grabbable_indices and \\\n                 k_idx not in world_data.workshop_indices and \\\n                 k_idx != world_data.water_index:\n                  return False  # This cell contains an impassable obstacle.\n      return True  # If no obstacles are found, the cell is traversable.\n\n  # Get the integer index for the target primitive from the environment's cookbook.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Access the current state of the environment.\n  state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Early exit: If the agent already has at least one of the primitive, no collection is needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # The 'collect' function is designed for items that go into the agent's inventory\n  # via a 'USE' action. If the primitive is not marked as grabbable, it cannot\n  # be collected this way.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve current state information necessary for pathfinding.\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) coordinates.\n  grid = state.grid      # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape # Dimensions of the grid.\n\n  # Get the integer action mappings for movement (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) and 'USE'.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION),\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION),\n  ]\n\n  # Identify all grid locations where the target primitive physically exists.\n  primitive_source_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_source_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map, it's impossible to collect.\n  if not primitive_source_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # Pre-calculate all \"interaction cells\" from which the agent can successfully\n  # perform a 'USE' action on the primitive. The 'USE' action affects a 3x3\n  # neighborhood around the agent's position (including the agent's cell).\n  target_interaction_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_source_locations:\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:  # Iterate for 3x3 neighborhood around primitive source\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n              # Add only valid grid coordinates to the set of target interaction cells.\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n                  target_interaction_cells.add((nx, ny))\n  \n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the\n  # agent's current position to any of the `target_interaction_cells`.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  # The 'visited' set tracks all positions already processed by BFS to prevent\n  # redundant computations and ensure the shortest path is found first.\n  visited = {agent_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # If the current position is one of the cells from which the primitive can be 'USED',\n      # we have found the shortest path. Append the 'USE' action and return the complete sequence.\n      if current_pos in target_interaction_cells:\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Use the helper function to determine if the next cell is traversable.\n          # This combines boundary checking and obstacle checking.\n          if not _is_traversable(next_x, next_y, grid, env.world):\n              continue  # Skip this position if it's out of bounds or an obstacle.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to ensure each branch of the BFS\n              # has its own independent path history.\n              new_path = list(path)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to an interaction cell was found,\n  # it means the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's initial position.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T01:20:03.792666", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  def _is_traversable(x: int, y: int, grid: np.ndarray, world_data: craft.CraftWorld) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"Helper function to determine if a given grid cell (x, y) is traversable.\n\n      A cell is traversable if it's within grid boundaries and does not contain\n      any impassable non-grabbable entities (e.g., walls, certain rocks, but not workshops or water).\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n      # Check grid boundaries first.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False\n\n      # Iterate through all possible kinds of entities at this cell.\n      for k_idx in range(num_kinds):\n          # If there's an entity of kind k_idx present at this cell.\n          if grid[x, y, k_idx] > 0:\n              # Check if it's a non-grabbable item.\n              if k_idx in world_data.non_grabbable_indices:\n                  # Special cases: workshops and water are typically traversable.\n                  if k_idx not in world_data.workshop_indices and k_idx != world_data.water_index:\n                      return False  # This cell contains an impassable obstacle.\n      return True  # If no impassable obstacles are found, the cell is traversable.\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the target primitive.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive)\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Pre-checks based on current state and primitive type.\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # If the agent already has at least one of the primitive, no collection is needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # The 'collect' function is specifically for items that can be picked up.\n  # If the primitive is not marked as grabbable, it cannot be collected using 'USE'.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Setup environment data.\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve integer mappings for all possible actions.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas and their corresponding actions for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION),\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION),\n  ]\n\n  # 4. Identify all cells on the grid where the target primitive is located.\n  primitive_source_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_source_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map, it's impossible to collect.\n  if not primitive_source_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Calculate \"target interaction cells\": positions from which 'USE' action works.\n  # The 'USE' action typically affects a 3x3 neighborhood around the agent.\n  target_interaction_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_source_locations:\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n              # Only add valid grid coordinates to the set of target cells.\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n                  target_interaction_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # Initialize BFS to find the shortest path.\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  visited = {agent_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # If the current position is a valid interaction cell, we've found the shortest path.\n      if current_pos in target_interaction_cells:\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighbors.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Check if the next position is traversable and hasn't been visited yet.\n          if _is_traversable(next_x, next_y, grid, env.world) and next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              new_path = list(path)  # Create a new path list for this branch.\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path was found to any interaction cell,\n  # the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T01:20:54.358460", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # Primitive name not recognized by the environment's cookbook.\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory. If so, no collection actions are needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Verify if the primitive is an item that can actually be 'grabbable' (picked up into inventory).\n  # Some items listed as \"primitives\" in the DSL (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP0)\n  # are environmental features not meant to be collected into inventory via 'USE'.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve current state information for pathfinding.\n  initial_pos = state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid.\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid_width, grid_height, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer action mappings from the environment for movement and 'USE'.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas and their corresponding action IDs for BFS.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION),\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION),\n  ]\n\n  # Identify all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # If the cell contains at least one unit of the target primitive.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Pre-calculate all \"target cells\" from which the 'USE' action can successfully\n  # interact with the primitive. This means any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # (including the center) of a primitive's actual location, as per CraftState.next_to.\n  target_use_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n              # Ensure the target 'use' cell is within the grid boundaries.\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n                  target_use_cells.add((nx, ny))\n\n  # Pre-calculate the set of kind indices that represent truly impassable terrain.\n  # A cell is considered impassable if it contains any non-grabbable entity\n  # that is NOT a workshop and NOT water. Workshops and water are typically traversable.\n  # This set will be used in the BFS to prune paths through obstacles.\n  impassable_entity_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  impassable_entity_kinds.difference_update(env.world.workshop_indices) # Workshops are traversable.\n  impassable_entity_kinds.discard(env.world.water_index) # Water is traversable.\n\n  # Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any cell that is a `target_use_cell`.\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])]) # Stores (current_position, path_taken_to_reach_here).\n  visited = {initial_pos} # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant computations.\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # If the current position is one of the pre-calculated target cells,\n      # we have found the shortest path. Append the 'USE' action and return.\n      if current_pos in target_use_cells:\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the next cell is traversable.\n          # A cell is impassable if it contains any kind from the pre-calculated impassable_entity_kinds.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Iterate only over the specific kinds that are known to be impassable for efficiency.\n          for k_idx in impassable_entity_kinds:\n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_impassable = True\n                  break\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this path if the cell is blocked by an impassable obstacle.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new list for the path to avoid modifying shared lists across BFS branches.\n              new_path = list(path) \n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to a target_use_cell is found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position given the current grid.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
