{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T01:26:53.174041", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid \n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # BFS setup\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  min_path_len = float('inf')\n  best_path_actions = []\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Get indices of known non-grabbable and special traversable items\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices # Contains all non-grabbables\n  workshop_indices = set(env.world.workshop_indices) # Convert to set for faster lookup\n\n  # Helper function to check if a primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of a given position\n  # This avoids creating a CraftState object repeatedly, improving performance.\n  def _is_next_to(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid, grid_width, grid_height):\n      cx, cy = check_pos\n      for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx_adj, ny_adj = cx + dx_adj, cy + dy_adj\n              # Check if the neighbor position is within grid boundaries\n              if 0 <= nx_adj < grid_width and 0 <= ny_adj < grid_height:\n                  # Check if the target primitive is present at this neighbor cell\n                  if current_grid[nx_adj, ny_adj, target_idx] > 0:\n                      return True\n      return False\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell is traversable.\n  # A cell is traversable if it doesn't contain any impassable object.\n  # Impassable objects are non-grabbable things that are not workshops AND are not the primitive we're looking to collect by being on it.\n  def _is_traversable(check_pos, target_primitive_idx, current_grid, non_grabbable_set, workshop_set):\n      cx, cy = check_pos\n      # Iterate through all kinds present at this position\n      for k_idx in range(N_KINDS):\n          if current_grid[cx, cy, k_idx] > 0: # If this kind is present at the cell\n              if k_idx in non_grabbable_set: # If it's a non-grabbable entity\n                  # If it's the primitive we are trying to collect by stepping ON it, it's traversable for this purpose.\n                  if k_idx == target_primitive_idx:\n                      continue \n                  # If it's a workshop, it's traversable (as workshops are locations to stand on).\n                  elif k_idx in workshop_set:\n                      continue\n                  # Otherwise, it's a non-grabbable, non-workshop, non-target-primitive kind\n                  # (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, STONE if not the target we want to stand on), \n                  # so it's considered an obstacle to movement.\n                  else:\n                      return False \n      return True # No impassable obstacles found at this position\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Pruning: If the current path is already longer than or equal to the best path found, \n    # then any further extensions of this path will also be longer, so we can skip.\n    if len(current_actions) >= min_path_len:\n        continue \n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), agent needs to be adjacent and then USE.\n      if _is_next_to(current_pos, primitive_idx, grid, WIDTH, HEIGHT):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    else: # Not grabbable (e.g., workshop, water, stone, boundary)\n      # For these, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, update the best path found so far\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      total_actions = current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n      if len(total_actions) < min_path_len:\n        min_path_len = len(total_actions)\n        best_path_actions = total_actions\n      # Do NOT break here immediately. BFS guarantees the shortest path to *a node*.\n      # However, our goal condition (reaching a node + potential USE action) means\n      # the overall shortest action sequence might be found through a different node\n      # reached at the same BFS depth, or even a node reached later in BFS if the\n      # `actions_to_complete_goal` makes it shorter overall. The `min_path_len`\n      # tracking correctly handles this.\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check if the new position is traversable and not yet visited\n        if _is_traversable(new_pos, primitive_idx, grid, non_grabbable_indices, workshop_indices):\n            if new_pos not in visited:\n                visited.add(new_pos)\n                q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  return best_path_actions", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T01:26:54.496156", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid # Access the grid directly\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  min_path_len = float('inf')\n  best_path_actions = []\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive for goal checking\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Get boundary index for obstacle checking. Handle cases where 'BOUNDARY' might not be defined.\n  boundary_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'] if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents else None\n  \n  # Check for special non-grabbable primitives like water, stone, boundary.\n  # Their \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  is_stationary_primitive = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             (boundary_idx is not None and primitive_idx == boundary_idx))\n  \n  # Helper function to check if a primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of a given position.\n  # This avoids instantiating `CraftState` objects repeatedly during BFS.\n  def _is_next_to(check_pos, target_idx, current_grid, grid_width, grid_height):\n      cx, cy = check_pos\n      for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx_adj, ny_adj = cx + dx_adj, cy + dy_adj\n              # Check if the neighbor position is within grid boundaries\n              if 0 <= nx_adj < grid_width and 0 <= ny_adj < grid_height:\n                  # Check if the target primitive is present at this neighbor cell (count > 0 means presence)\n                  if current_grid[nx_adj, ny_adj, target_idx] > 0:\n                      return True\n      return False\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if _is_next_to(current_pos, primitive_idx, grid, WIDTH, HEIGHT):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, update the best path found so far.\n    # We continue BFS even after finding a goal to ensure the globally shortest path,\n    # as other paths might lead to a goal with fewer total actions (including the final USE).\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      total_actions = current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n      if len(total_actions) < min_path_len:\n        min_path_len = len(total_actions)\n        best_path_actions = total_actions\n      # Do NOT break here. BFS finds the shortest path to *a state in the search graph*.\n      # Our goal might be achieved via multiple states, and the first one found might not\n      # correspond to the shortest sequence of actions (especially if `ACTION_USE` is involved).\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        is_impassable_cell = False\n        # Obstacle check: If the new cell contains 'BOUNDARY' and the target primitive is NOT 'BOUNDARY'.\n        # Agents cannot move into 'BOUNDARY' cells unless 'BOUNDARY' itself is the target to collect.\n        if boundary_idx is not None and grid[new_x, new_y, boundary_idx] > 0 and primitive_idx != boundary_idx:\n            is_impassable_cell = True\n\n        # If the new position is valid, not visited, and not an impassable obstacle, add it to the queue.\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_cell:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive is unreachable or blocked by obstacles),\n  # or if a path was found, return the shortest one.\n  return best_path_actions", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T01:27:44.159092", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n\n  This version refines the pathfinding and interaction logic to ensure robust collection\n  of primitive items in the CraftWorld environment. It leverages Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  to find the shortest path to a location from which the primitive can be 'used' (collected).\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation state.\n      primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to be collected (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of integer action codes (e.g., UP, DOWN, USE) to navigate to\n                 the primitive and collect it. Returns an empty list if the primitive is\n                 not found or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Access current state and environment details\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's (x, y) tuple position\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # 2. Map primitive name to its integer ID\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized by the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Get integer mappings for all relevant actions from the environment's action space.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement actions and their corresponding (dx, dy) deltas.\n  # This mapping is used for BFS exploration.\n  movement_actions = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1),\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  # 4. Get grid dimensions\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Last dim is n_kinds, not needed for width/height\n\n  # 5. Identify terrain types that block agent movement.\n  # In CraftWorld, \"WATER\" and \"BOUNDARY\" are typically considered impassable obstacles.\n  blocking_terrain_indices = set()\n  if 'WATER' in cookbook.index.contents:\n    blocking_terrain_indices.add(cookbook.index['WATER'])\n  if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents:\n    blocking_terrain_indices.add(cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  \n  # Helper function: Determines if a given grid cell is within bounds and traversable.\n  def is_traversable(x: int, y: int) -> bool:\n    # Check if coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False\n    \n    # Check if the cell contains any blocking terrain.\n    # A cell is blocked if it contains *any* of the blocking_terrain_indices.\n    for blocking_idx in blocking_terrain_indices:\n      if grid[x, y, blocking_idx] == 1: # Check if the blocking kind is present at (x,y)\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 6. Locate all instances of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # `np.argwhere` returns (x, y) coordinates where `grid[:, :, primitive_idx]` is 1.\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n\n  if len(primitive_locations_on_grid) == 0:\n    # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it's impossible to collect.\n    return []\n\n  # 7. Pre-calculate all grid cells from which the agent can successfully `USE`\n  # to collect the target primitive.\n  # An agent can `USE` a primitive if it's in an adjacent cell (including diagonals,\n  # i.e., Chebyshev distance <= 1).\n  valid_use_spots = np.full((grid_width, grid_height), False, dtype=bool)\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive location.\n    for dx_use in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_use in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        ux, uy = px + dx_use, py + dy_use\n        # Mark the cell (ux, uy) as a valid `USE` spot if it's within grid bounds.\n        if 0 <= ux < grid_width and 0 <= uy < grid_height:\n          valid_use_spots[ux, uy] = True\n\n  # 8. Initial Check: Is the agent already positioned on a `valid_use_spot`?\n  # If so, the only action needed is 'USE'. This is the most efficient scenario.\n  if valid_use_spots[agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1]]:\n    return [ACTION_USE]\n\n  # 9. Pathfinding using Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # BFS finds the shortest path in an unweighted graph (our grid).\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_x, current_y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n  \n  # `visited` set keeps track of grid cells already added to the queue to prevent cycles\n  # and redundant exploration, ensuring the shortest path is found first.\n  visited_cells = {agent_pos} \n  \n  while bfs_queue:\n    (current_x, current_y), actions_to_current = bfs_queue.popleft()\n\n    # Explore all four possible movement directions from the current cell.\n    for action_type, (dx, dy) in movement_actions.items():\n      next_x, next_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy  # Calculate potential next position\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the next position is traversable and has not been visited yet.\n      if is_traversable(next_x, next_y) and next_pos not in visited_cells:\n        actions_to_next = actions_to_current + [action_type]\n        \n        # If the next position is a `valid_use_spot`, a path has been found.\n        # Since this is BFS, this path is guaranteed to be the shortest.\n        if valid_use_spots[next_x, next_y]:\n          return actions_to_next + [ACTION_USE] # Append the 'USE' action and return the full path.\n        else:\n          # If not a `valid_use_spot` yet, add this new position to the queue\n          # for further exploration and mark it as visited.\n          visited_cells.add(next_pos)\n          bfs_queue.append((next_pos, actions_to_next))\n        \n  # 10. If the BFS completes and no path to a `valid_use_spot` was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the agent's current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
