{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T02:57:43.167335", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world # Access to cookbook, grabbable/non-grabbable indices\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_inventory = current_state.inventory\n  agent_initial_pos = current_state.pos\n  agent_initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent direction not crucial for static pathfinding, but needed for CraftState init\n\n  # 1. Map the primitive string name to its unique integer ID.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized by the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Early exit: If the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory,\n  # no further actions are needed to \"collect\" it.\n  if agent_inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Retrieve integer IDs for all possible actions from the environment.\n  action_ids = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_ids['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_ids['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_ids['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_ids['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_ids['USE'] # Used for interacting with grabbable items or workshops\n\n  # 4. Define possible movement vectors (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # This simplifies iterating through neighbors in the BFS.\n  MOVE_ACTIONS = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases Y-coordinate)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y-coordinate)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X-coordinate)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # 5. Get grid dimensions to ensure agent stays within bounds.\n  GRID_WIDTH, GRID_HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 6. Initialize the Breadth-First Search (BFS) data structures.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(agent_initial_pos, [])])\n  # The visited set keeps track of positions already explored to prevent cycles and redundant paths,\n  # ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited_positions = {agent_initial_pos}\n\n  # 7. Categorize the target primitive based on its collection mechanism.\n  is_grabbable_item = primitive_idx in world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in world.workshop_indices\n  # Passive collectibles (e.g., water, stone, boundary) are \"collected\" by merely reaching their cell.\n  is_passive_collectible = (primitive_idx == world.water_index or\n                            primitive_idx == world.stone_index or\n                            primitive_idx == cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n\n  # 8. Perform BFS to find the shortest path to the primitive.\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_actions = queue.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and the path leading to it.\n\n    # Create a temporary CraftState instance for the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState methods (like `next_to`) or directly query the grid\n    # as if the agent were physically at `current_pos`, without altering the actual environment state.\n    temp_check_state = craft.CraftState(\n        scenario=current_state.scenario,\n        grid=grid,\n        pos=current_pos,\n        dir=agent_initial_dir,\n        inventory=agent_inventory\n    )\n\n    # Check if the current position satisfies the goal for collecting the primitive.\n    if is_grabbable_item:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., 'WOOD', 'IRON'), the agent must be adjacent to them\n      # and then perform a 'USE' action to pick them up.\n      if temp_check_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        # BFS guarantees this is the shortest path to an adjacent cell.\n        # Append the 'USE' action and return the complete sequence.\n        return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop_location or is_passive_collectible:\n      # For workshops (e.g., 'WORKSHOP0', 'BENCH') or passive collectibles ('WATER', 'STONE', 'BOUNDARY'),\n      # \"collection\" means simply reaching the cell where the primitive is located.\n      # Check if the primitive is directly present at the current cell's location in the grid.\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        # This is the shortest path to a cell containing the primitive.\n        # No 'USE' action is needed; just reaching the location suffices.\n        return path_actions\n\n    # Explore valid neighboring cells (up, down, left, right) from the current position.\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVE_ACTIONS:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if 0 <= new_x < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < GRID_HEIGHT:\n        # Avoid revisiting positions already explored to guarantee the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n        if new_pos not in visited_positions:\n          visited_positions.add(new_pos)\n          # Enqueue the new position along with the extended path.\n          queue.append((new_pos, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # 9. If the BFS completes and no path to the primitive was found (e.g., the primitive\n  # does not exist on the map or is completely unreachable), return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T02:58:34.195662", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by pre-calculating impassable entity kinds and optimizing target detection.\n\n    This function uses Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence of\n    movement actions to reach a position from which the target primitive can be\n    collected using the 'USE' action.\n\n    A 'USE' action is effective if the agent is within a 3x3 square centered\n    on the target primitive's location (i.e., on the same cell or one cell away\n    orthogonally or diagonally).\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list of action integers (from `env.action_specs()`) representing\n                   the shortest path to collect the primitive. Returns an empty list\n                   if the primitive is not found in the environment or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Map the primitive name to its integer index using the environment's cookbook.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name does not correspond to a known item, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Extract necessary state information from the current environment state.\n  state = env._current_state\n  initial_pos = state.pos  # Agent's starting (x, y) coordinates\n  grid = state.grid        # The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 3. Get the integer action IDs from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs for BFS exploration.\n  move_deltas_and_actions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION),  # Move one cell down (increase y)\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION),   # Move one cell up (decrease y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION), # Move one cell left (decrease x)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION), # Move one cell right (increase x)\n  ]\n\n  # Pre-calculate the set of entity kinds that truly act as impassable obstacles.\n  # These are non-grabbable entities that are NOT workshops and NOT water,\n  # meaning the agent cannot move onto them. The primitive itself (if it's non-grabbable)\n  # should also not be an obstacle for movement, only for collection.\n  true_impassable_kinds = (\n      set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) -\n      set(env.world.workshop_indices) -\n      {env.world.water_index}\n  )\n\n  # 4. Find all locations on the grid where the target primitive currently exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          # Check if the primitive kind's layer at (x, y) has a non-zero count.\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map, no collection is possible.\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, [])])\n  # The visited set stores positions (x,y) to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {initial_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      cx, cy = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is within the 'USE' range of any primitive location.\n      # The 'USE' action works if the agent is in the 3x3 neighborhood (including the cell itself).\n      is_within_use_range = False\n      for px, py in primitive_locations:\n          # Calculate Chebyshev distance (max of dx, dy) for 3x3 neighborhood check.\n          if max(abs(cx - px), abs(cy - py)) <= 1:\n              is_within_use_range = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_within_use_range:\n          # If a suitable position is found, append the 'USE' action and return the complete path.\n          path.append(USE_ACTION)\n          return path\n\n      # Explore all four possible neighboring cells from the current position.\n      for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_and_actions:\n          next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # First, check if the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds\n\n          # Second, determine if the next cell is traversable.\n          is_impassable = False\n          # Iterate through all possible kinds/layers at the next cell.\n          for k_idx in range(grid.shape[2]): \n              if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If something of kind `k_idx` is present at this cell.\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx:\n                      # Agent can move onto the primitive itself to collect it. It is traversable.\n                      continue \n                  # Check if the present kind is one of the pre-computed true obstacles.\n                  if k_idx in true_impassable_kinds:\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # Found an obstacle, no need to check further kinds in this cell.\n\n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Skip this next position if it's blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # If the cell is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Create a new path list by extending the current path.\n              new_path = list(path)\n              new_path.append(action_id)\n              queue.append((next_pos, new_path))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
