{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T04:56:03.314605", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid # Current grid state\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # OPTIMIZATION: If the agent already has the primitive, no actions are needed to collect it.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Get correct action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up (Y decreases)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down (Y increases)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left (X decreases)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right (X increases)\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Identify \"impassable\" kinds. Assume 'BOUNDARY' is an obstacle.\n  impassable_kind_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'] if 'BOUNDARY' in cookbook.index.contents else None\n\n  # --- Determine possible sources and their collection actions ---\n  # This section defines what grid entities can yield the 'primitive'\n  # and what action is required (e.g., USE, or just reaching the cell).\n  \n  # List of (kind_idx, action_type_str) tuples, where action_type_str is 'use' (needs adjacency + USE)\n  # or 'reach' (needs to be on the cell, no extra action).\n  target_sources = [] \n\n  # Case 1: Primitive is directly grabbable from the grid\n  # These are items that can be picked up using ACTION_USE when adjacent.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    target_sources.append((primitive_idx, 'use'))\n\n  # Case 2: Primitive is a stationary environmental element or a workshop\n  # For these, 'collecting' means simply reaching their location on the grid.\n  if (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n      primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n      primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices):\n    target_sources.append((primitive_idx, 'reach'))\n  \n  # Handle BOUNDARY as a primitive if it's the target itself (e.g., reaching a boundary cell).\n  if impassable_kind_idx is not None and primitive_idx == impassable_kind_idx:\n      target_sources.append((impassable_kind_idx, 'reach'))\n\n  # Case 3: Primitive is obtained by harvesting a source entity with ACTION_USE\n  # This mapping is based on typical CraftWorld mechanics where some primitives\n  # are derived from other entities on the grid (e.g., WOOD from TREE).\n  # We look up the source entity (e.g., 'TREE' for 'WOOD').\n  # These source names must exist in the cookbook.index.\n  harvest_sources_map = {\n      'WOOD': 'TREE',\n      'IRON': 'IRON_ORE',\n      'GRASS': 'GRASS_PLANT',\n      # Extend this map for other harvestable primitives if known (e.g., 'ROCK': 'ROCK_VEIN')\n  }\n  \n  source_name_for_primitive = harvest_sources_map.get(primitive)\n  if source_name_for_primitive:\n    source_kind_idx = cookbook.index.get(source_name_for_primitive)\n    if source_kind_idx is not None:\n      target_sources.append((source_kind_idx, 'use'))\n\n  # If no known way to obtain this primitive is identified, return an empty list.\n  if not target_sources:\n      return []\n\n  # Helper function to check if any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood around current_pos\n  # contains the target_kind_idx.\n  def _is_next_to(current_x, current_y, target_kind_idx):\n    for dx_neighbor in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_neighbor in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        # Exclude the agent's current position (center of 3x3 neighborhood)\n        if dx_neighbor == 0 and dy_neighbor == 0:\n          continue\n        \n        nx, ny = current_x + dx_neighbor, current_y + dy_neighbor\n        \n        # Check if neighbor is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT:\n          # Check if the target kind is present in this neighboring cell (count > 0)\n          if grid[nx, ny, target_kind_idx] > 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # Visited set to keep track of positions already processed to avoid redundant exploration\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n    current_x, current_y = current_pos # Unpack for direct grid access and next_to logic\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for any of the target sources\n    for target_kind_idx, action_type in target_sources:\n      is_goal_reached = False\n      actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n      if action_type == 'use': # Requires agent to be adjacent to target_kind_idx, then ACTION_USE\n        if _is_next_to(current_x, current_y, target_kind_idx):\n          is_goal_reached = True\n          actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n      elif action_type == 'reach': # Requires agent to be on the cell with target_kind_idx\n        if grid[current_x, current_y, target_kind_idx] > 0:\n          is_goal_reached = True\n          actions_to_complete_goal = []\n      \n      # If a goal state is reached, return the path immediately.\n      # For an unweighted graph, BFS guarantees the first path found to a goal state is the shortest.\n      if is_goal_reached:\n        return current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Check for obstacles: do not move into a 'BOUNDARY' cell\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        if impassable_kind_idx is not None:\n            # If the new position contains a 'BOUNDARY' and the target is NOT 'BOUNDARY' itself, it's an obstacle.\n            if grid[new_x, new_y, impassable_kind_idx] > 0 and (primitive_idx != impassable_kind_idx):\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n\n        if new_pos not in visited and not is_impassable_obstacle:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If BFS completes and no path is found (e.g., primitive or its source is unreachable)\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T04:57:15.002414", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # (px, py) where px is column, py is row\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  world = env.world # Shorthand for easier access to world attributes\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive not found in the cookbook, return empty actions\n    return []\n\n  # Get action integer mappings\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # If the agent is already next to the primitive, no movement is needed, just use it.\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # Find all occurrences of the primitive on the grid.\n  # grid[:, :, primitive_idx] extracts a 2D slice.\n  # np.argwhere returns (x_coord, y_coord) for the specific kind in that slice.\n  primitive_target_coords = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n  \n  # If the primitive is not present on the grid, we can't collect it.\n  if len(primitive_target_coords) == 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine which kinds are considered impassable for agent movement.\n  # Agent cannot path onto these cells, it must path *around* them.\n  impassable_kinds = set()\n  \n  # The primitive itself is generally impassable for direct movement;\n  # agent must stand *next* to it to collect.\n  impassable_kinds.add(primitive_idx)\n\n  # Water is typically an impassable terrain feature.\n  if world.water_index is not None:\n      impassable_kinds.add(world.water_index)\n  \n  # Stone is also often an impassable terrain feature.\n  if world.stone_index is not None:\n      impassable_kinds.add(world.stone_index)\n\n  # Other non-grabbable entities that are not workshops are typically impassable (e.g., boundaries).\n  # Workshops are explicitly treated as walkable.\n  for kind_idx in world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      is_workshop = False\n      for ws_idx in world.workshop_indices:\n          if kind_idx == ws_idx:\n              is_workshop = True\n              break\n      if not is_workshop:\n          impassable_kinds.add(kind_idx)\n\n  # BFS setup\n  q = collections.deque()\n  visited = set() # To store (x, y) coordinates already visited by BFS\n\n  # Start BFS from the agent's current position\n  # Queue stores (current_x, current_y, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q.append((agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1], []))\n  visited.add(agent_pos)\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding actions\n  # dx affects x-coordinate (column), dy affects y-coordinate (row)\n  movements = [\n      (0, -1, UP),    # Move up (decrease y-coordinate)\n      (0, 1, DOWN),   # Move down (increase y-coordinate)\n      (-1, 0, LEFT),  # Move left (decrease x-coordinate)\n      (1, 0, RIGHT)   # Move right (increase x-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  while q:\n    curr_x, curr_y, path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current position is adjacent to any primitive location.\n    # An agent at (curr_x, curr_y) is adjacent to (target_x, target_y) if\n    # their Chebyshev distance is 1 (i.e., |curr_x - target_x| <= 1 AND |curr_y - target_y| <= 1).\n    is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n    for target_x, target_y in primitive_target_coords:\n      if abs(curr_x - target_x) <= 1 and abs(curr_y - target_y) <= 1:\n        is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n        break\n    \n    if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n      # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell! Append USE action and return.\n      path_actions.append(USE)\n      return path_actions\n\n    # Explore valid neighbors\n    for dx, dy, action in movements:\n      new_x, new_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n      # 1. Check grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= new_x < grid_width and 0 <= new_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Out of bounds\n\n      # 2. Check if this new position has not been visited yet in the BFS\n      if (new_x, new_y) in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Check if the cell (new_x, new_y) is walkable (does not contain impassable objects)\n      is_walkable_cell = True\n      \n      # Get all entity kinds present at (new_x, new_y) in the grid (assuming one-hot encoding per cell)\n      entities_in_cell = np.where(grid[new_x, new_y, :] == 1)[0]\n      \n      if len(entities_in_cell) > 0: # Cell is occupied by one or more entities\n          # First, check if it's a workshop (workshops are always walkable, even if non-grabbable)\n          is_a_workshop = False\n          for ws_idx in world.workshop_indices:\n              if ws_idx in entities_in_cell:\n                  is_a_workshop = True\n                  break\n          \n          if is_a_workshop:\n              is_walkable_cell = True # It's a workshop, so it's walkable\n          else:\n              # If not a workshop, check if it contains any explicitly impassable kind\n              for entity_kind_at_cell in entities_in_cell:\n                  if entity_kind_at_cell in impassable_kinds:\n                      is_walkable_cell = False # It contains an object that blocks movement\n                      break\n      # If entities_in_cell is empty, is_walkable_cell remains True (empty cells are walkable)\n\n      if is_walkable_cell:\n        visited.add((new_x, new_y))\n        q.append((new_x, new_y, path_actions + [action])) # Create a new list for the path\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable or not present given current obstacles.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T04:57:16.309012", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # (px, py) where px is column, py is row\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the primitive\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive not found in the cookbook, return empty actions\n    return []\n\n  # Get action integer mappings\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # If the agent is already next to the primitive, no movement is needed, just use it.\n  # This uses the built-in `state.next_to` which is likely optimized.\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # Check if the primitive exists anywhere on the grid. If not, it's unreachable.\n  if not np.any(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1):\n      return []\n\n  # BFS setup\n  q = collections.deque()\n  visited = set() # To store (x, y) coordinates already visited by BFS\n\n  # Start BFS from the agent's current position\n  # Queue stores (current_x, current_y, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q.append((agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1], []))\n  visited.add(agent_pos)\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding actions\n  # dx affects x-coordinate (column), dy affects y-coordinate (row)\n  movements = [\n      (0, -1, UP),    # Move up (decrease y-coordinate)\n      (0, 1, DOWN),   # Move down (increase y-coordinate)\n      (-1, 0, LEFT),  # Move left (decrease x-coordinate)\n      (1, 0, RIGHT)   # Move right (increase x-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  while q:\n    curr_x, curr_y, path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Optimized Adjacency Check:\n    # Check if any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood around (curr_x, curr_y) contains the primitive.\n    # This avoids iterating over all primitive locations found on the map,\n    # instead directly checking the local grid around the current BFS position.\n    is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n    for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        check_x, check_y = curr_x + dx_adj, curr_y + dy_adj\n        # Check boundaries for the neighboring cell\n        if 0 <= check_x < grid_width and 0 <= check_y < grid_height:\n          if grid[check_x, check_y, primitive_idx] == 1:\n            is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n            break # Found a primitive in the 3x3 neighborhood\n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n        break # Break outer loop too\n\n    if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n      # Found the shortest path to a cell adjacent to the primitive! Append USE action and return.\n      path_actions.append(USE)\n      return path_actions\n\n    # Explore valid neighbors\n    for dx, dy, action in movements:\n      new_x, new_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n      # Check grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < grid_width and 0 <= new_y < grid_height:\n        # Check if this new position has not been visited yet\n        if (new_x, new_y) not in visited:\n          visited.add((new_x, new_y))\n          q.append((new_x, new_y, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable or not present.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T04:58:32.859251", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook, cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # If the primitive is already in inventory and is a grabbable item, no actions are needed.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices and state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] \n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movements (dx, dy) and their corresponding action IDs\n  MOVES = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Up\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Down\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Left\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Right\n  ]\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n\n  # Pre-cache common indices and type determinations for efficiency\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Determine if the primitive is a \"stationary\" one (water, stone, boundary)\n  # For these, collecting means simply reaching the cell where they are.\n  water_idx = env.world.water_index\n  stone_idx = env.world.stone_index\n  boundary_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'] # Can be None if 'BOUNDARY' is not in the cookbook\n\n  is_stationary_primitive = (\n      primitive_idx == water_idx or \n      primitive_idx == stone_idx or \n      (boundary_idx is not None and primitive_idx == boundary_idx)\n  )\n  \n  # For grabbable items, we need to find the shortest path that includes a 'USE' action.\n  # This might mean checking multiple adjacent locations.\n  min_path_len = float('inf') \n  best_path_actions = [] \n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Optimization: If the current path length already equals or exceeds the best found for a grabbable item,\n    # we can prune this path as it won't be shorter. This does not apply to stationary items/workshops,\n    # as we return immediately upon finding them.\n    if is_grabbable and len(current_actions) >= min_path_len:\n      continue \n\n    # Create a hypothetical CraftState at the current BFS position.\n    # This allows us to use CraftState's `next_to` method or check `grid` contents\n    # as if the agent were actually at `current_pos`.\n    # Agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect pathfinding geometry.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Check if this `current_pos` represents a goal state for collecting the primitive\n    is_goal_reached = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, update the best path found so far\n    if is_goal_reached:\n      if is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n        # If the target is a stationary primitive or workshop, and we've reached it,\n        # this is the shortest path due to BFS property. Return immediately.\n        return current_actions \n      elif is_grabbable:\n        # For grabbable items, we found a way to be adjacent and USE.\n        # Store this path if it's shorter, but continue BFS to find potentially shorter paths\n        # by being adjacent to *other* instances of the primitive.\n        total_actions = current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n        if len(total_actions) < min_path_len:\n          min_path_len = len(total_actions)\n          best_path_actions = total_actions\n        # Continue BFS, don't return here.\n\n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVES:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Determine if the new position is impassable.\n        # A cell is considered impassable if it contains any entity from the\n        # `non_grabbable_indices` set, AND that entity is NOT the primitive we are trying to collect.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        for non_grabbable_kind_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n          if grid[new_x, new_y, non_grabbable_kind_idx] > 0 and non_grabbable_kind_idx != primitive_idx:\n            is_impassable_obstacle = True\n            break # Found an obstacle, no need to check other non_grabbables for this cell\n        \n        if is_impassable_obstacle:\n          continue # Skip this cell as it's an impassable obstacle\n\n        if new_pos not in visited:\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # If the BFS queue is exhausted, return the best path found for grabbable items.\n  # If no path was found (e.g., primitive not on the map or unreachable), \n  # best_path_actions will be empty, which is the correct behavior.\n  return best_path_actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T04:58:34.035146", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left)\n  }\n  ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR = {}\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Early exit: If the grabbable primitive is already in inventory.\n  # This applies only to items that increase inventory count (grabbables).\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices and state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] \n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Populate ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR based on action_map\n  ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR[ACTION_UP] = (0, -1, 0)    # Up, North\n  ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR[ACTION_DOWN] = (0, 1, 2)   # Down, South\n  ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR[ACTION_LEFT] = (-1, 0, 3)  # Left, West\n  ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR[ACTION_RIGHT] = (1, 0, 1)  # Right, East\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current position and direction\n  start_pos = state.pos\n  start_dir = state.dir # Initial direction matters now for USE action\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, current_direction_int, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])]) \n  # Visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to avoid redundant exploration of same state\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)} \n\n  # Cache common indices and type determinations outside the loop for efficiency\n  boundary_idx = cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'] \n\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  # A primitive is stationary if it's water, stone, or boundary (and boundary itself is the target)\n  is_stationary_primitive = (\n      primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n      primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n      (boundary_idx is not None and primitive_idx == boundary_idx)\n  )\n  \n  # For grabbable items, we need to find the shortest path that includes a 'USE' action.\n  min_path_len = float('inf') \n  best_path_actions = [] \n  \n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_dir, current_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # Pruning: If the current path length already equals or exceeds the best found,\n    # we can stop exploring this path for grabbable items.\n    # For stationary/workshop items, we return immediately upon finding the first path,\n    # so this pruning is primarily for grabbables where we seek the shortest path *to any valid (pos, dir) + USE*.\n    if is_grabbable and len(current_actions) >= min_path_len:\n        continue \n\n    # Determine actions needed to complete goal from current (pos, dir)\n    is_goal_reached_at_current_state = False\n    actions_to_complete_goal = []\n\n    if is_grabbable:\n        # For grabbable items, the agent must be facing the item and then USE.\n        front_dx, front_dy = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n        target_cell_x, target_cell_y = current_pos[0] + front_dx, current_pos[1] + front_dy\n\n        # Check if the cell directly in front is within bounds and contains the primitive\n        if 0 <= target_cell_x < WIDTH and 0 <= target_cell_y < HEIGHT and \\\n           grid[target_cell_x, target_cell_y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n            is_goal_reached_at_current_state = True\n            actions_to_complete_goal = [ACTION_USE]\n            \n    elif is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n      # For workshops, water, stone, or boundary, \"collecting\" means reaching the location itself.\n      # Check if the target primitive is present at the current cell.\n      if grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        is_goal_reached_at_current_state = True\n        actions_to_complete_goal = [] # No USE action is typically needed for these\n    \n    # If a goal state is reached, update the best path found so far\n    if is_goal_reached_at_current_state:\n      total_actions_len = len(current_actions) + len(actions_to_complete_goal)\n\n      if is_workshop or is_stationary_primitive:\n        # If the target is a stationary primitive or workshop, and we've reached it,\n        # this is the shortest path due to BFS property. Return immediately.\n        return current_actions \n      \n      elif is_grabbable:\n        # For grabbable items, we found a way to position and orient the agent for USE.\n        # Store this path if it's shorter, but continue BFS to find potentially shorter paths\n        # as there might be other instances of the primitive or shorter paths to them.\n        if total_actions_len < min_path_len:\n          min_path_len = total_actions_len\n          best_path_actions = current_actions + actions_to_complete_goal\n        \n    # Explore neighbors of the current position\n    for action_id, (dx, dy, new_dir) in ACTION_TO_DELTA_DIR.items():\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # Determine if the new position is impassable.\n        # A cell is impassable if it contains a 'BOUNDARY' entity AND the 'BOUNDARY'\n        # is NOT the primitive we are trying to collect. This allows collecting 'BOUNDARY' itself.\n        is_impassable_boundary = (\n            boundary_idx is not None and \n            grid[new_x, new_y, boundary_idx] > 0 and \n            primitive_idx != boundary_idx\n        )\n        \n        if is_impassable_boundary:\n          continue # This cell is occupied by a boundary and is thus impassable for current goal\n\n        # Check if this (new_pos, new_dir) state has been visited\n        if (new_pos, new_dir) not in visited:\n          visited.add((new_pos, new_dir))\n          q.append((new_pos, new_dir, current_actions + [action_id]))\n  \n  # If the BFS queue is exhausted, return the best path found for grabbable items.\n  # If no path was found (e.g., primitive not on the map or unreachable), \n  # best_path_actions will be empty, which is the correct behavior.\n  return best_path_actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T04:59:56.225878", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid # Current state of the world grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive] \n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Retrieve integer mappings for actions from the environment's specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement actions in terms of (delta_x, delta_y, action_id).\n  MOVE_ACTIONS = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move agent Up (decreases Y-coordinate)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move agent Down (increases Y-coordinate)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move agent Left (decreases X-coordinate)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Move agent Right (increases X-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # Get grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, number_of_kinds).\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Agent's current starting position.\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Categorize the primitive to apply appropriate collection logic.\n  is_grabbable_item = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  is_immobile_environment = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \n                             primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index or \n                             primitive_idx == cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'])\n  \n  # --- Immediate Check: Optimize for collection possible from the current position. ---\n  temp_state_at_current_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, start_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n  \n  if is_grabbable_item:\n    if temp_state_at_current_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n      # Agent is already adjacent to a grabbable item, just needs to USE it.\n      return [ACTION_USE]\n  elif is_workshop_location or is_immobile_environment:\n    if temp_state_at_current_pos.grid[start_pos[0], start_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n      # Agent is already on the same cell as the workshop or immobile env element.\n      # No further action needed; it's considered \"collected\" by being there.\n      return []\n\n  # Determine the minimum number of additional actions needed *after* reaching a collection point.\n  # For grabbable items, a 'USE' action is typically required. For others, just being on the spot suffices.\n  min_actions_to_complete_collection = 1 if is_grabbable_item else 0\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS):\n  # The queue will store tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # A set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant processing.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Variables to store the shortest sequence of actions found so far.\n  min_total_actions_len = float('inf')\n  shortest_path_actions = []\n\n  # BFS loop: Continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while q:\n    current_pos, current_actions = q.popleft()\n    current_path_len = len(current_actions)\n\n    # Optimization: Prune this path if it's already too long or cannot lead to a shorter solution.\n    # If the current path length plus the minimum actions to complete collection\n    # is already greater than or equal to the best path found so far,\n    # then this path cannot be the shortest.\n    if current_path_len + min_actions_to_complete_collection >= min_total_actions_len:\n      continue # This path is already too long or will be.\n\n    # Create a hypothetical `CraftState` object at the `current_pos`.\n    # This allows us to use `CraftState` methods (like `next_to`) to check conditions\n    # as if the agent were actually at this position, without modifying the real environment state.\n    # The agent's direction and inventory are kept constant as they don't affect grid-based pathfinding for location.\n    temp_state_at_pos = craft.CraftState(state.scenario, state.grid, current_pos, state.dir, state.inventory)\n\n    # Determine if the primitive can be 'collected' from the `current_pos`.\n    # This acts as the goal condition for our BFS.\n    goal_met_at_current_pos = False\n    # Actions that might be needed *after* reaching `current_pos` to complete collection (e.g., USE).\n    post_movement_actions_for_collection = []\n\n    if is_grabbable_item:\n      # For items that can be picked up (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be adjacent to them and then USE.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.next_to(primitive_idx):\n        goal_met_at_current_pos = True\n        post_movement_actions_for_collection = [ACTION_USE]\n    elif is_workshop_location or is_immobile_environment:\n      # For workshops or environmental features, \"collecting\" means being on the same cell as the item.\n      # We check if the target primitive is present at the `current_pos`.\n      if temp_state_at_pos.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive_idx] > 0:\n        goal_met_at_current_pos = True\n        post_movement_actions_for_collection = [] # No additional action like USE is required.\n\n    # If the goal condition is met at the current position, evaluate this path.\n    if goal_met_at_current_pos:\n      total_path_candidate = current_actions + post_movement_actions_for_collection\n      # If this path is shorter than any previously found path, update the shortest path.\n      if len(total_path_candidate) < min_total_actions_len:\n        min_total_actions_len = len(total_path_candidate)\n        shortest_path_actions = total_path_candidate\n      # We do NOT `break` here. BFS guarantees the shortest path to a *node*.\n      # However, our \"goal\" might involve an action (like `USE`) taken from a node,\n      # and multiple nodes (e.g., different adjacent cells) could satisfy the condition.\n      # We must continue the BFS to ensure we find the absolute shortest *sequence of actions*\n      # that leads to successful collection. The pruning condition above helps accelerate this.\n\n    # Explore valid neighbors of the current position.\n    for dx, dy, action in MOVE_ACTIONS:\n      new_x, new_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n      new_path_len = current_path_len + 1 # Length of path to new_pos\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if 0 <= new_x < WIDTH and 0 <= new_y < HEIGHT:\n        # If the new position has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n        if new_pos not in visited:\n          # Further pruning: Only add this path to the queue if it could potentially\n          # lead to a shorter overall solution than the best one found so far.\n          if new_path_len + min_actions_to_complete_collection < min_total_actions_len:\n            visited.add(new_pos)\n            q.append((new_pos, current_actions + [action]))\n  \n  # Return the shortest sequence of actions found to collect the primitive.\n  return shortest_path_actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
