{"timestamp": "2025-08-02T07:34:03.952330", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  agent_pos = state.pos  # (px, py) where px is column, py is row\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not recognized by the cookbook.\n    return []\n\n  # Get integer mappings for actions\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # --- Optimization: Check if already next to the primitive ---\n  # If the agent's current position is already within the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # of the primitive, we only need to perform the USE action.\n  if state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # --- Step 1: Find all actual primitive locations on the grid ---\n  # np.argwhere returns a list of (x, y) coordinates where the primitive_idx layer is 1.\n  primitive_on_grid_coords = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n  \n  # If the primitive isn't anywhere on the grid, it's unreachable.\n  if len(primitive_on_grid_coords) == 0:\n    return []\n\n  # --- Step 2: Pre-calculate all potential agent 'USE' positions ---\n  # These are all the grid cells from which the agent can successfully perform a 'USE' action.\n  # A 'USE' position is any cell (px, py) such that a primitive exists in the\n  # 3x3 neighborhood centered at (px, py).\n  potential_use_positions = set()\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  for target_x, target_y in primitive_on_grid_coords:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive location.\n    # The agent can USE from any cell in this neighborhood.\n    for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        adj_x, adj_y = target_x + dx_adj, target_y + dy_adj\n        \n        # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= adj_x < grid_width and 0 <= adj_y < grid_height:\n          potential_use_positions.add((adj_x, adj_y))\n  \n  # --- Step 3: Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) for the shortest path ---\n  # BFS will find the shortest sequence of move actions to reach any cell\n  # in `potential_use_positions` from the agent's current location.\n  q = collections.deque()\n  visited = set() # Stores (x, y) coordinates that have been added to the queue\n\n  # Initial state for BFS: (current_x, current_y, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q.append((agent_pos[0], agent_pos[1], []))\n  visited.add(agent_pos)\n\n  # Define possible movements and their corresponding actions\n  movements = [\n      (0, -1, UP),    # Change in y: -1 (move UP)\n      (0, 1, DOWN),   # Change in y: +1 (move DOWN)\n      (-1, 0, LEFT),  # Change in x: -1 (move LEFT)\n      (1, 0, RIGHT)   # Change in x: +1 (move RIGHT)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    curr_x, curr_y, path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current BFS position is one of the pre-calculated 'potential_use_positions',\n    # we have found the shortest path to a valid 'USE' location.\n    if (curr_x, curr_y) in potential_use_positions:\n      # Append the USE action and return the complete action sequence.\n      path_actions.append(USE)\n      return path_actions\n\n    # Explore valid, unvisited neighboring cells.\n    for dx, dy, action in movements:\n      new_x, new_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries.\n      # (Assuming all cells within boundaries are traversable; CraftWorld typically handles this.)\n      if 0 <= new_x < grid_width and 0 <= new_y < grid_height:\n        # Check if this new position has not been visited to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n        if (new_x, new_y) not in visited:\n          visited.add((new_x, new_y))\n          # Add the new position and the updated path to the queue.\n          q.append((new_x, new_y, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to a 'potential_use_position' was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current agent position.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
